#passage(("There are multiple types of evidences that we use. Number one, we can say, is the miraculous nature of the Quran itself. So the Quran has a challenge that has been given to the Arabs, that has been given to everyone until the end of time: imitate the Quran, produce something like it. First the challenge was: bring something like the Quran. Then the Arabs couldn't. Nobody could. The Quran has a very unique structure in the Arabic language. So in the Arabic language you have [prose], you have poetry; the Quran has its own unique genre. So the Arabs [had] the highest level of understanding of the Arabic language at the time. The Quran came in Arabic, and [it] challenged [them] to produce similar structures to the Quran.", "This is an objective criteria. You have Christian Arabs, millions of them. You have Jewish Arabs. You have Arabic professors who are here in England who are non-Muslims. All of them, you can go to them, say to them, \"Can you produce something like the structure of the Quran? Do you agree that this is the highest literature form in the Arabic [language]?\" All of them will admit to you that this is the case. And we can know, because we can study every chapter. There's a book written, and it has every chapter: what makes it unique, what are the unique structures in it that you can imitate, and show us something like it if you're able to. So it's an objective criteria for anyone who understands the Arabic language and its eloquency, so that can be anyone who speaks Arabic. It doesn't have to be a Muslim to take that challenge. And the Quraysh, by the way, that time they were the highest people in the Arabic language; that was their specialtity. That's why that challenge came in the Arabic language. None of them were able to imitate it. Until today, you don't have any single example of anyone who were able to imitate or meet the challenge of the Quran.", "If you're an expert in whichever language it is, and I produce to you a scripture that has a specific grammatical structure, has a specific combination of words, etc., and I say, \"Imitate it, bring something like it\", and if you do, then that's proof I'm not a prophet of god. The Quran says: if you don't believe that this scripture is from God, then bring something like it. It's a challenge of the Quran. It says: bring a booklet like it. It challenged the Arabs to do that and they couldn't do it, and that [challenge is] until the end of times. It's not only for the Arabs. Even today you have AI, you have all of these things, and nobody have been able to do it. There are people who use language AI, and the language AI told you that they cannot imitate the Quran. So either way, that's a fact, that's a reality. Until it's been done, you cannot refute the challenge. Nobody can do this. If someone does this, then we can talk.", "We have the Quran. We don't have Jesus. We can observe the grammatical eloquence and miracle of the Quran today. So it's not the same: one you can see with your own eyes and appreciate it; one is already gone 2,000 years ago. It's not the same, so you cannot make that claim; that's a false comparison.", "The prophecies of prophet Muhammad: prophet Muhammad has made tens of prophecies, if not hundreds of prophecies, about the future, clear, specific.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Three Confident Christians Attempt To Take On A Muslim! Mohammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lbP6og-VXmE", ((2476, "41:16–41:54"), (2526, "42:06–43:05"), (2592, "43:12–44:51"), (2697, "44:57–45:18"), (2724, "45:24–45:33"),))
