#passage(("I'd like you to keep two things in mind in regards to the topic of eloquence. It's very important that, when you're attempting the Quran's challenge (of course, I'm speaking to critics of Islam), it can't be stupid. You can't have stupid statements; stupidity doesn't fit in with eloquence. If it's stupid, it fails a challenge. It's a very simple criteria: don't be stupid. You can't say, \"It's certain death, go wash your hands.\" Secondly, don't sacrifice meanings for the sake of rhyme. And this is something that many attempts fall into, and this is one of the harder things, I guess: trying to come up with a good rhyme without sacrificing meaning. Poets fall into this error, and they always get called up for it. Even modern poets, ancient poets, they all get called out for sacrificing the meaning for rhyme.", "This was not attempted by the people of Makkah. This was not attempted by the greatest poets during the time of Rasulullah. Instead, you had the greatest poets of the time convert to Islam. I wonder why.",), "Farid Responds, “Response to Surah Corona / Covid”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e9vuXIg5kE8", ((682, "11:22–12:32"), (755, "12:35–12:51"),))

