#passage(("The Quran that the Prophetﷺ came with: he came with a Quran that is the most eloquent speech in the Arabic language, because the Arabs at that time, what they were known with was the Arabic language, and the Quran came as a challenge for them in that field of theirs. So they cannot come and make an excuse and say, \"We don't know what that is, we don't know what this is.\" And you had many of them saying \"this is magic\": speech, language that we speak, they say this is magic, because of how miraculous the Quran was. Those Arabs, they're specialised in the field; that's why they went to the extent of saying \"this is magic\". Many of us don't properly understand the nature, the magnificence of the Quran; that's why we're not understanding why they would say that, or go to the extent of saying this is magic.", "And the Quran was a challenge for them to produce something like it, meaning the structure of the Quran, the prophecies, everything, the eloquence, all of these things in the Quran, because it's introduced new things into the Arabic: new words into Arabic language, used previous words in the Arabic language that was not known before, introduced new grammatical structures into the language, introduced new combinations of words into the language. To put it to you the simplest way, it is like me speaking to you in English, using English letters, but I'm using new grammatical structures. Now, you know, the verb comes after this, it ends with the I-N-G, and I'm not doing that; I'm using a complete new grammatical structure. I'm using the same letters as you. And I'm using words that you never heard before, but you understand the meaning I'm telling you. And I'm using old words that you know the meaning of in a new way, and you completely understand the new meaning that I'm using. And I'm combining words in the language, in grammar, in a new way you've never encountered before, and you still understand them.", "In Surat alFatiha, for example, Allahﷻ says: (alFatiha1:1-7) بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَـٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ (In the name of Allah, The-Most-Gracious, The-Most-Merciful), if you want to use that translation, even though this is a lot more of explanation between arRahman, arRaheem. Both arRahman arRaheem are taken from the root word Rahma (mercy). Now, have you ever heard in history, in any language, someone introduced: \"In the name of the king, the most great, the very great\"? No, because you do not go and introduce someone, in any language, let alone Arabic, where you introduce someone and you praise him with attributes, more than one after the other, take it from the same root, too. It did not exist in the language of the Arabs. Then to say الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ: this Alhamdu, الحمدُ (praise), was never used by the Arabs with AL, الـ, alAlif and alLam, which is letters of identification, which means the whole Praise and whole Gratitude is due to Allahﷻ. They've never used that before in their poetry, alHamdu with the Alif and Lam in the beginning of their speech. And then Allahﷻ says: مَالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ (The Owner of the Day of Judgement). Are you aware of the owner of the hour? The owner of the year? The owner of the week? Have you ever heard this term before? \"Owning time\" is a concept that humans do not even think about. But The Creator owns everything, including time. That's why this description, it shows you its divinity when you speak about it; shows you that this is coming from The Creator of everything, The Owner of everything, because Allahﷻ owns Time. And the Day of Recompense, or the Day of Debt: we know the day of the event, the day of the match; we don't know this concept of \"the Day of Debt\" or \"the Day of Recompense\", and we don't even use that in language, other languages, even not the Arabic. I'm giving you these things, and you're even seeing the miraculous nature in English, let alone Arabic.", "There's a beautiful Book written on that called \"المعجزة: إعادة قراءة الإعجاز اللغوي في القرآن الكريم\" للدكتور بسام ساعي (Re-Reading The Linguistic Miracles In The Noble Quran), and it's called \"The Miracle\", by Dr Bassam Sa'ei, in English, I believe. But the translation, I didn't like it much, and it's not the full book, because it's a very heavy Arabic language topic. And this is an objective challenge, objective measurement. Every chapter I can do this with: I can show you the new words there, the new usages, all of these things, and that's what Dr Bassam Sa'ei does. He gives you actual examples, and he gives you the objective criteria. This is not a subjective criteria based on language, like \"Shakespeare sounds good\". No, there's objective criteria: every chapter has this one, two, three, four, five. These criteria: present something like it using the Arabic language and Arabic letters.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Islam Unveiled: Compelling Evidence For The Truthfulness Of Islam | Chicago - USA | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUFsBco_CF0", ((1296, "21:36–22:20"), (1345, "22:25–23:44"), (1429, "23:49–25:51"), (1559, "25:59–26:38"),))
