#passage(("The Quran itself: you might not speak the [Arabic] language, but you can still rely on the fact that every Arab today will tell you the Quran is the highest Arabic literature that cannot be imitated. And they have no reason to say that: if they could bring an alternative, or if anyone in human history was able to bring an alternative, they would have adopted the alternative; the Arabs would not be Muslims, especially with the technology. And this funny thing is that people go to AI and say, \"Can you imitate the Quran?\", and then language AI tells them no. AI is just codes that are input by a human being; it's not going to be able to imitate anything, because you cannot imitate the Quran. It's as simple as that.", "Allah says \"Malik\", the owner of the day of judgment. We own physical things; we don't own time. But the one who created the universe does own time, because he created time. So when you read these things, you realize that they are descriptions of a Creator, not descriptions that can come from a human being, because these Concepts do not even come through your mind while you're speaking. So I'll say, very simply: anyone who's sincere cannot reject the reality that Islam is the truth.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Pakistani Ex-Muslim Confronts A Muslim On Following Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9vJWVgYof2A", ((572, "9:32–10:17"), (686, "11:26–12:00"),))
