#passage(("That challenge has been there for 1400 years; no one has been able to replicate it. The very funny thing: whoever tried to bring something, they've been mocked, because what they did is copying the style of the Quran, and they just changed the words. They took some words from here and they put it there. This is plagiarism; it's not imitation. The Quran has a very objective criteria of how it can be imitated, and they couldn't do it.", "First, why did the miracle come in the Arabic language? The reason the miracle came in the Arabic language was because the Arabs were advanced the most in Arabic. This was their prime. We will never come back to the prime of the Arabic language of that time. And Allah gives miracles in the things that people are specialised in. Moses brought a miracle that showed the Magicians, because they specialised in magic, that this was something bigger than Magic. In the time of Abraham, they used to burn people, so Abraham was thrown in the fire and he didn't burn. So Allah gives a miracle that the people would understand, things that they're specialised in, that they would know. So Allah brought the Quran in the Arabic language as a miracle, as a book, for that reason.", "Now, what the Arabs did is that they sent the best poets of their time. They sent Alwalid ibn Almughira, 'Utbah ibn Rabi'ah; these are the poets they sent, the biggest of the time. They said, \"Go see what this man is saying.\" Imagine you being at the peak of the Arabic language, then you have the biggest poets of the time going to the prophet to test him. One of them said this is Magic. When you say something is magic, you're saying that something is supernatural, meaning you cannot do it; you cannot imitate it. And another person gave a very beautiful description of the Quran. He said: \"It rises and nothing rises above it, and it shatters everything under it.\" This is a disbeliever, and he stayed a disbeliever. He could not speak, he could not answer. He went