#passage(("Every Chapter has this criteria: new words, new constructs, words that were never used before, or words used differently in every Chapter of the Quran. That's why the Quran2:23 claims \"Bring a Chapter like it\". So imagine now someone constructing all of these things that I'm telling you, and he is bringing revelation that he didn't prepare for. People come and ask him questions, and revelation comes down, and he instantly responds. For example, Allah says: \"وَيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الرُّوحِ\", they ask you about the الروح (Rooh); the Prophet responds with revelation: \"قُلِ الرُّوحُ مِنْ أَمْرِ رَبِّي\", say the Rooh \"The Soul is of the Affair of my Lord. وَمَا أُوتِيتُم مِّنَ الْعِلْمِ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا\" (Quran17:85): \"And you have not been given except a little of The Knowledge\". They come and they ask him: يَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْأَهِلَّةِ (Quran2:189), they ask you about moon changing. وَیَسۡـَٔلُونَكَ عَنِ ٱلۡمَحِیضِۖ, they ask you about menstruation: قُلۡ هُوَ أَذࣰى, say it is harm, so stay away from women in the period of menstruation, and the Quran2:222 comes down. Some of it was circumstantial, some of it was questions being asked, some of it was in war. Can a human being actually do that, in a period of 23 years, and not contradict himself, not a single time?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Arab Christian Introduced To The Challenge Of The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n-flvFktgzU", ((287, "4:47–5:57"),))
