#passage(("I've just watched a video by David Wood in which he was making arguments against the Quran. I'd actually say: yes, go see what the experts say. The problem here is that David is so disconnected from Arabic and from the field of eloquence and the relevant literature, he's got no idea who the experts are. I actually have a list of experts in Arabic eloquence, old and contemporary, Muslim and non-Muslim, that have praised the Quran, and yes, I even have examples of Christian Arabs who have referred to the Quran as miraculous. Here's an example of French orientalist [Mardrus], who translated much of the Quran as well as the Thousand One [Nights] into French, and he completely agrees that the Quran is both magnificent and divine in its style. But I'll be frank: I'm not going to be calling him an expert simply because he has a view that is in line with mine, and unfortunately that seems to be David's criteria: if he can use your position, then that person, whoever he is, is definitely an expert.",), "Farid Responds, “David Wood Challenged me to Refute this Video”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o6MinzBhq5o", ((1, "0:01–2:02"),))

