#passage(("The claim that Arabic is the best language for the Quran isn't a claim that's just made up. Christian [Orientalist] M. makes the same argument: he claims that the effects of the Quran cannot be expressed in a similar manner in any other language, especially his very own French. According to alii, who David claims is an expert, the beauty of the Arabic cannot be reproduced in another language. Let me give you something better: Arthur Arbury, the head of the Department of Classics at University of Cairo in Egypt once upon a time, and the translator of the Quran, says that \"the rhetoric and Rhythm of the Arabic of the Quran are so characteristic, so powerful, so highly emotive, that any version whatsoever is bound in the nature of things to be but a poor copy of the glittering splendor of the original. Never was it more true than in this instance that [traduttore, traditore].\" This is a common Italian expression; it means the translator is a traitor. So the idea is that if the translator translates something, he's going to mess up the meaning, or he's not going to be 100% accurate to what the original text says.",), "Farid Responds, “Why Quran was Revealed in Arabic? [Response to David Wood]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VzKfYtuwWG8", ((228, "3:48–5:51"),))
