#passage(("You have two options when it comes to looking into the claims of the Quran being a miracle, and yes, the second one is definitely a lot harder. But you see, the thing is that previous physical Miracles are not even accessible to you: you've never seen the sea split and you never will, and you've never seen the raising of the dead and you never will. Islam provides you with a miracle that you can actually access. However, again, it's not the easiest thing to do in the world, and you're going to have to spend a good amount of time studying the material. And then you have option one, which is relying on the statements of the experts in the field. Now I know what you're thinking. You're saying, \"But why should I believe in these testimonies?\" Well, aren't you already believing in the testimonies of those that spoke about the splitting of the sea and those that spoke about the raising of the Dead? If you believe those testimonies, then why are you rejecting the testimonies of those that have claimed that Quran is a miracle of eloquence? In most cases, the claims of these classical or ancient physical Miracles aren't even by eyewitnesses; they're by Anonymous authors, or even late authors that are allegedly quoting eyewitnesses.", "So here's what I'm offering: the Quran is a text that came with a challenge to produce something like it. The Arab pagans, instead of coming with something like it, instead of challenging the Quran, what they did was they actually converted to Islam. They changed their religion, they stopped believing in the gods they believe in, they adopted a whole new way of life. Now, folks like David might say something like, \"Oh yeah, well, those people, those poets, they converted to Islam because they were forced to, because of the wars and whatnot.\" And of course, in response to that, I would have to ask: which Wars caused the forced conversions?",), "Farid Responds, “David Wood Challenged me to Refute this Video”", "https://www.youtube.