d the Jews. Then Waraqa ibn Nawfal confirmed it to the Prophetﷺ; he told him that \"that angel that came to you is the same angel that came to Moses\", i.e. he brought to you Revelation. And that was one of the only one or two times the Prophetﷺ met Waraqa ibn Nawfal, because he passed away later on. A lot of Christians seem to think that the Prophet took the Quran from Waraqah ibn Nawfal, even though at the first encounter of Revelation Waraqa was not there, and he died straight away after.", "Then Angel Gabriel came to the Prophetﷺ, and other parts of the Quran were revealed, like Surah alMuddathir, where Allahﷻ commanded the Prophetﷺ to deliver the Message. So first, was to recite the Quran. That's why the word القرآن (the Quran) is taken from reciting or reading. This is how the Quran is meant to be understood and transmitted: it is primarily an Oral Text, and the main way of preserving the Quran was through the oral tradition; it was not through the written text. The written text was always looked at as a secondary source.", "Then the Quran came down gradually over a period of 23 years, as Allahﷻ mentions in the Quran (alisraa17:106): وَقُرْءَانًۭا فَرَقْنَـٰهُ لِتَقْرَأَهُۥ عَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ عَلَىٰ مُكْثٍۢ (and the Quran that we divided so you can recite it gradually on the people), so people can gradually take it in, embrace it, and understand it. Circumstantial events took place, and then the Quran was revealed talking about them, etc.", "And whenever any part of the Quran came down, the Prophetﷺ always commanded someone to write it down, like Uthmanؓ mentioned in his narration, that whenever any part of the Quran was revealed, the Prophetﷺ brought someone to write the Quran down, and he told him where to place these specific verses through the Revelation. There was multitude of different people who are called -specifically- كتبة الوحي (Writers of Revelation). These people were people the Prophetﷺ selected, and whenever the Quran came down, he called one of the