#passage(("Prophet Muhammad did not read or write, as majority of the people in that time. People 1,400 years ago, especially in Arabia, were not literate people, generally. There were not schools and institutions. So, it wasn't like that Prophet Muhammad alone was like this. That was the majority of the community. But the Quran was revealed in 23 years. Every time a verse was revealed of the Quran, the Prophet Muhammad brought one of his companions to write it down instantly in his life.", "Who wrote it down? We have the names of the writers of revelation, over 50 companions. We have Uthman ibn Affan, we had Zayd ibn Thabit, we had Ali ibn Abi Talib. I can go on and on. I'll give you who these people were, what was the relationship of Prophet Muhammad, the lineage, tracing back to Ishmael. When were they born? When did they die? Who were these people? I'll give you all of this. When Prophet Muhammad passed away, the entire Quran was written down, in whatever they had. They had parchments, they had leather pieces, rocks; whatever they had they could write on in that time, they wrote the Quran on.", "And then the third caliph comes, Uthman ibn Affan. And Islam spread far and wide in the beginning, in the first 80 years. So, there were so many new people accepting Islam. So, now, there were people reading the Quran, new converts of Islam making mistakes in the Quran, and people disagreeing with each other, because they're far away from the mainland. They're far away from where the revelation was sent out. At that time, we're talking about nearly 30 years after Prophet Muhammad.", "So, what he did is he said: \"We're going to keep the original, which is preserved, and then we're going to standardize it.\" And then he made copies of it, around six copies. He sent it to all the different Muslim regions. And he sent with every one of them a teacher, so people can know the exact recitation, so they don't make mistakes. And the original ones, did Uthman burn them after? No,