#passage(("The Bible that you have today, it has been changed by men. There's [interpolations] and additions to it. This is according to Christian scholars, leave Muslim scholars. Bruce Metzger is a conservative Christian scholar; he wrote a book called \"The Text of The New Testament: Its Transmission, Corruption, and Restoration\", and he admits in the book that we don't know who wrote this book, we cannot know for sure; it has been changed throughout history. If you read Bart Ehrman, he has a book called \"Misquoting Jesus\"; he says the same thing. He used to be a Christian, textual criticism scholar, and he left Christianity.", "There is an oral tradition of memorising the full Quran. Millions of Muslims memorise the Quran; they read it every day in their Prayer. Every Ramadan, we recite the whole Quran in the Mosque, any Mosque you'll go to, 30 parts in the 30 days. This tradition has been there from the beginning, so the Quran is a living tradition. If you throw every Book in the sea, you cannot change it. But not only that, we have written Manuscripts from the time of the Prophet: Birmingham Manuscript here, it's from the life of the Prophet. If you go to San'aa, there's a San'aa Manuscript from the 1st Century; Topkapi manuscript from the 1st century. So we know for a fact, the Quran is preserved.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Iceland Visitors Enquire About Islam! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xigQO8G9dOo", ((805, "13:25–13:51"), (847, "14:07–14:43"),))
