#passage(("You can never find a translation of the Quran that has verses that are not in another translation. You cannot find a translation of the Quran that claims some of the verses of the Quran does not exist in the earliest manuscript. You're trying to apply the Biblical idea to the Quran, and it will never happen, because the Quran is a set number of chapters, a set number of verses, and they're the same. And the translations will always give the same meaning; they're not going to give different meanings. Open any translation you like: you'll see the wording can be different, but the meaning is the same.", "Anyone can go and open Quran.com, open Pickthall translation, Abdul Haleem Translation, Saheeh International Translation, any translation you want, and then they will see they're all saying the same thing. You're not going to find a single one of them that will say to you these verses here, from 9 to 20, they don't exist: they exist in Pickthall, but they don't exist in Saheeh International. It's a false comparison that you're trying to make, because you have a problem with manuscripts. We don't have a problem with manuscripts, because we have a set number of chapters and verses. We don't have a translation that has 66 chapters of the Quran, one that has 73, and one that has 82. This is your problem. The problem is when you project this problem into that. It doesn't work, because it's not there.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Preacher Claims To Have Evidence For Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YRJIE9cDck0", ((1492, "24:52–25:13"), (1542, "25:42–26:17"),))
