#passage(("Now, there's a story about a Jewish rabbi. It was at the time of [al-Ma'mun], I believe. And he saw this Jewish rabbi: there was a sitting, there was a gathering, and he sat down, and he was very eloquent in speech, very intelligent. So he said to him: \"Why don't you become Muslim?\" So then he refused. Then a year later, that same Jewish rabbi again in a sitting, and now he's speaking about Islam. So he asked him, \"Did you become a Muslim?\" \"Yeah, I became a Muslim.\" \"I invited you to Islam a year ago. Why did you accept Islam now? What happened? What changed?\"", "So he says that he did an experiment. He took the Tawra books of the Jewish people, and he said: \"I changed here and there, taking some of here, adding some books here. And then I went to the synagogue. I gave it to the rabbis. They bought it from me. Nobody was like: wait, this is not our book, this is not a Torah, what is this?\"", "He says he did the same thing: went to the Christian church. He took the Bible, changed, put some things here, take some things here. If you buy a copy of the Bible 10 years ago and you compare it to the one today, it already has changes. I'm not going to talk to you about one 2,000 years ago. He gave them their book. He already corrupted and changed it. Nobody knows. He said: \"I tried the same on the Quran. I went to the memorizers, and they threw it in my face.\" That was the reason he accepted Islam. He understood nobody can corrupt this preservation of this faith, the preservation of this religion. Nobody can come anywhere close to it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How Do You Know Which Religion Is From God? A Detailed Comprehensive Analysis | The Muslim Lantern”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9F5gS1yWIRI", ((1575, "26:15–27:20"), (1640, "27:20–27:45"), (1665, "27:45–28:32"),))
