#passage(("So, after that gradual Revelation was coming down and the Prophetﷺ commanded people to write parts of the Quran, then Islam started to spread within the Deserts of Arabia. The Arabs at that time had multitude of different dialects, just like today: you can look at the English, or whichever language you want to look at; you have different people in different parts of the world, they're all speaking English, but they are speaking different dialects of the same language. So, that was the same case for the Arabs at the time.", "When Islam spread to different Arab tribes, like Tameem, etc., it was difficult for these other tribes, that speak other dialects other than the dialect of Quraysh (which was the first dialect that the Quran was revealed in), to recite the Quran in a dialect other than their own. After Islam spread in all of these different tribes, there was a need for the Quran to also be easier for these people, because in these people you have the very old man, you have the very young child, and you have different people among them that cannot speak the dialect of Quraysh.", "So the Prophetﷺ, he spoke with Angel Gabriel, he requested. He said (Bukhari:3219): فَلَمْ أزَلْ أسْتَزِيدُهُ. I asked Angel Gabriel to ask Allah to make an easy way for those individuals that are from different tribes that cannot speak the dialect of Quraysh. So what happened is that Allahﷻ revealed the Quran in 7 different dialects, which are also known as \"the 7 Ahruf\", so Allahﷻ can make it easier for the people to recite the Quran in their own dialect.", "As the Hadith says, the Prophetﷺ said (Muslim:819): فَلَمْ أزَلْ أسْتَزِيدُهُ (I kept requesting him to increase until he gave me 7 Ahruf). And then Allahﷻ said: whichever Harf (dialect) you would recite the Quran in, from these 7 dialects, you're correct, فَقَدْ أَصَابُوا (You're correct). There is no problem. Allahﷻ also gave the command (alMuzzamil73:20): فَٱقْرَءُوا۟ مَا تَيَسَّرَ مِنْهُ (Recite whatever is easy for you). So you can recite from these different dialects whatever is comfortable, whatever is easy for you as an individual, because the whole reason for the Quran to be revealed in these seven different dialects was to make it easy for the people!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The History Of The Quranic Text| A Breakdown From Revelation To Compilation| Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JjBR2JbHN6o", ((424, "7:04–7:27"), (452, "7:32–8:17"), (502, "8:22–8:44"), (536, "8:56–9:25"),))
