// U FR263:205-229 | Farid Responds | 1
#passage(("[Ibn Qutaybah] specifically says: \"And some of them wanted to return to the origins and recite in every dialect.\" In other words, the reciter would repeat the same verse again and again in different dialects, and he would say: this is a dialect of this tribe, and that is a dialect of that tribe. So [Ibn Qutaybah] is not condemning the attribution of recitation [to] dialects; rather, he's condemning those that are reciting words over and over again within one recitation.",), "Farid Responds, “Yasir Qadhi: \"The Standard Narrative has Holes\" - A Response to Orientalists”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B0GGbZeGQOw", ((525, "8:45–9:19"),))
// U FR076:144-160 | Farid Responds | 1
#passage(("So the prophet, peace be upon Him, is in Mecca for the majority of his prophethood; he only has [Meccans] around him. Why would he be reciting in different dialects in the first place? As David correctly pointed out, it was during the time [of Hisham's] acceptance of Islam that Omar first realized that there are multiple modes. Well, the natural assumption is that these multiple modes were revealed very late into the [prophethood], and that makes sense, because that's when you had multiple tribes from different regions converting to Islam.",), "Farid Responds, “David Wood Fails to Refute me on Qiraat”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6KsYZK-YGEI", ((342, "5:42–6:18"),))
