#passage(("This is example three-one. There seems to be something going on with the name of Allah: seems as if it has been inserted into text, as [Brubaker] has mentioned. This is from the Marcel manuscript; it's dated to the 8th century.", "So what we did was very simple. We found (and by the way, this stuff is all available online) other manuscripts that were from the same time. This is also from before the year 800. And what we did here is we zoomed into the image, and we've identified the inclusion of the name of Allah, like our present text, and here is an image from a modern printed Quran for you to make that comparison. We did this with multiple examples: here's one from Cairo; here's one from Yemen, this one also from before 800; here's another one, I believe this is in Germany, it's quite early, [649] to [675]; here's one from France, once again the name of Allah.", "It might be tough in the beginning getting used to reading Arabic manuscripts, but you get used to it with time. When I first started off, it took me ages to read a single page.", "Notice there are no corrections in these manuscripts. The name of Allah exists in all of these, which shows again it's the same exact verse that Brubaker was showing, and this is proof that the text was not flexible, but that the original example was a mistake. We've shared eight examples for this specific example.",), "Farid Responds, “Were Early Quran Manuscripts Manipulated?”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZD1-epRprFc", ((1159, "19:19–19:37"), (1177, "19:37–20:45"), (1247, "20:47–20:57"), (1409, "23:29–23:59"),))
