#passage(("Brubaker says that the job of thorough and deep analysis of these thousands of changes is not something that one person can necessarily take on. And that's his excuse for not comparing his examples to the examples that we've shared: for example, the eight examples of the same verse that included the word Allah. He didn't go through that because it's just too much work.", "Now the issue is, we're not asking Daniel to go through manuscripts to compare the thousands of changes. He should have done this for the 20 that he's published a book about. If you're putting this information forward as a small sample of information, the simplest thing you could do is just go online and make sure that this argument is water tight. I don't know what it is: is it laziness, is there something more to it? I'll leave that for the imagination of the audience.", "You'd be surprised to hear: what took him eight years to collect, it took us about eight days to collect all this data, a bit less, and the rest was formatting, because you have to zoom in and do all of that.",), "Farid Responds, “Were Early Quran Manuscripts Manipulated?”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZD1-epRprFc", ((1598, "26:38–27:15"), (1646, "27:26–28:06"), (1778, "29:38–29:52"),))
