#passage(("Brubaker has been making a name for himself for collecting scribal errors and displaying them as examples for the lack of preservation of the Quran. So if any scribe in the history of Islam made an error in copying a word, then that means the [Quran] is not preserved.", "Now the issue with that, Dan: I don't know if you've really learned much about textual criticism, but this is referred to as [dittography], which is the mistaken repetition of a word or a letter by a copyist. That's all it is. And how do we know that this is just a mere scribal error and not an actual original? First of all, the word is repeated, and the fact that it's repeated implies that the copyist [forgot] the word that he wrote earlier and he rewrote it again. This form of a mistake is so common it actually has a name: [dittography]. Look it up, Dan.", "Secondly, how do we know that this isn't a part of the original? Because other manuscripts, some of which were written earlier, don't include this same mistake. How many years of your life you waste gathering these scribal errors!",), "Farid Responds, “11 Differences in 1 page of Quran (Response to David Wood)”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JmjURdYS5K0", ((690, "11:30–12:00"), (810, "13:30–14:34"), (874, "14:34–15:36"),))
