#passage(("Let's highlight one thing which is very important. Just because there's similarities in historical literature, there's similarities in the Quran, and they both are mentioning something similar, it doesn't mean that one copied from the other. And that's why we're going to tell the Christians: why don't you apply the same standard to your book? For example, you have the idea of the flood of Noah, and you have this idea of the flood in the Epic of Gilgamesh. So why don't we say then that the Bible is copying the Epic of Gilgamesh? They would never say this. They would say: oh no, there's a similarity just because it happened, someone recorded it. They would make up all sorts of excuses. The Bible is full of all of these kind of traditions that come from pagan teachings and pagan beliefs. And then the Christians will argue: oh no, the writers of the Bible would never copy pagan rituals. And they would come with all sorts of justifications for things which are similar in paganism and within Christianity. So they always play this hypocrisy, double standard, when it comes to that.", "Now, when it comes to the idea of the infancy gospel, that text which was the earliest Arabic translation we have of it is from 1299 AD or something, way after Prophet Muhammad. But there is a Syriac manuscript of it. How did Prophet Muhammad get that Syriac text? Where is your proof? It's all claims: just because two things are saying the same thing, then one is copied from the other. And the Prophet Muhammad, how did he learn Syriac or Arabic? Where is he getting this information from? There's plenty of works that are labeled as Apocrypha that are not mentioned in the Quran.", "And then you have the Bible mentioning certain statements, and the Quran mentions certain statements. If Prophet Muhammad is a messenger from God, he's saying the same stories of the prophets. God is revealing to him what he revealed to Jesus, what he revealed to Moses, and what he revealed to all the prophets. So when the New Testament quotes the Old Testament, cuz the Old Testament is before the New Testament, people say: oh, this is from the same God. Even though the Jews don't accept that. They will tell you: no, your religion is not a continuation of Judaism. But you will argue that because they're coming from the same God, it's fine for these parallels to exist. Why don't you apply the same standard when it comes to the Quran?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Wess Huff Claims The Quran Was Copied From The Bible | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hb-kHiXbGxI", ((782, "13:02–13:58"), (839, "13:59–14:32"), (872, "14:32–15:08"),))
