#passage(("My point is very simple. Whoever calls it Apocrypha, it's just Christians who came later on who identified as Apocrypha, which is completely useless for us from a Muslim point of view; this is history for us. Us confirming whether it happened or not is based on whether the Quran is from God or not. So I don't care about what the Apocrypha says, I don't care what the Bible says. I look at the Quran as a Scripture on its own: does it have evidence? Why do I need to look at the Quran in the lens of Apocrypha or what the Bible says? To me that's ridiculous. I look at it as its own Scripture.", "The Quran is not saying to you: go research the Torah and the Gospel and the Old Testament and the Bible and Apocrypha, and then come believe in me. The Quran is saying: this is the Book from God. Believe in this Book. Take the Book as it is. This Book is sufficient for you. So that's what we're saying. We look at the Quran the way it is. We don't have this twisted idea that we need to prove the Quran through previous scriptures that existed.", "So for me, just because history records these things, it's just more evidence that these things happened. But why do I believe they happened? It's because I have independent evidence that the Quran is from God. I don't need to look at the Bible to begin with. The Bible is useless for me, not from any offensive point of view; I'm saying from a Muslim point of view. For me to believe in Islam, I did not need to look into the Bible at all. I looked at Islam for what it is. I looked at the Bible way later on, and Christian history and this and that, to engage with other people. But for me to become a Muslim, it was enough the evidences that the Quran provides to show that this is from God.", "It's irrelevant what the Apocrypha says, it's irrelevant what the Old Testament says. What is relevant is: this Scripture holds its own as evidence that is from God to begin with or not? If it does, and it can be proven to be from God, and I have evidences that Prophet Muhammad is the Prophet of God, then I would accept whatever he says, because I have evidence that he's a Prophet of God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Claims The Quran Is Historically Plagiarised! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ngAbQzpSvMw", ((240, "4:00–4:36"), (276, "4:36–4:55"), (300, "5:00–5:27"), (332, "5:32–5:47"),))
