#passage(("When he lived with these people for 40 years, he wasn't traveling, spending his time in Christian countries learning from rabbis and priests.", "He was like 13 years old, traveled one time with his uncle. Someone recognized him, or signs that he was a prophet, and told him to go, because if the Jewish people find him, they're going to harm them. So they left instantly. There was a priest or a rabbi or someone that saw him and noticed some signs of prophethood on the prophet, something to do with him and the shade, if I remember correctly.", "Now, is it possible for him to learn all of these type of things when he traveled once when he was 13 years old? So he wasn't going back and forth. There's no record of the Prophet Muhammad doing that whatsoever.", "In Mecca, there were not Jewish and Christian communities for the first 13 years of revelation. Then the Prophet Alaihis Salat Was Salam went to Medina, and then the situation is different in Medina, which is the last 10 years of his life.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Confident Agnostic Grills A Muslim On The Quran Copying The Bible! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=24D1h0UflFg", ((501, "8:21–8:28"), (522, "8:42–9:23"), (594, "9:54–10:06"), (630, "10:30–10:42"),))
