#passage(("The Rosetta Stone is a stone that we discovered in 1799, I believe, or 1899, one of the two, like 200 or 300 years ago, not that long ago. That Rosetta Stone contains a language called Hieroglyphics. It's translated to the Demotic language and then translated into the Greek language. We started reading Hieroglyphics only after the discovery of the Rosetta stone. Before that we couldn't read what is in the pyramids! So, if the Prophet traveled EVERYDAY to Egypt and went inside the pyramids every day (which there's no historical record of that, because he was living with his people: people would see him travel and go back and forth; the deserts were very clear, deserts of Arabia, everyone will know you went somewhere and came back; people were living in neighborhoods!), even if he did that, it's not going to help him, because he cannot read the Hieroglyphics. He doesn't know what the symbols mean; we only discover that after the Prophetﷺ, over a thousand years after the Prophet. So your argument here doesn't work.", "This is what atheists do, with all due respect, not you, but many atheists do this all the time. Atheists will say Prophet Muhammadﷺ was an Astronomer. He was a psychologist, he was a biologist, he was an astrologist, he was a geologist. He had all knowledge in history of all different languages, including Greek, including Aramaic, including knowledge of the previous scriptures. He was the most genius, so he could bring a perfect system and a structure for humanity. He also had, somehow, knowledge of the future and access to know what is going to happen in the future!", "I'm making the claim that in order for what you're saying to be true, he needs to have all of these things. The reason why this HAS to be the case is because Islam has information about all of these things, and if it was true that Prophet Muhammad was doing what you're saying he was doing, he was going around and doing hearsay, the Quran would be full of false information, because he would get wrong information and true information. How can you determine that what people are telling you is true or not? You're just going to listen, you're going to take the information and say it to the people. So, if what you're saying was the case, the Quran would be full of mistakes, especially scientific mistakes, because the people believed the most absurd and ridiculous things at the time. For instance, that's why the Hindu scripture reflects absurd beliefs, like there's a bull with his two horns holding the Earth (YajurVeda 4-30), there are seven horses pulling (RigVeda 1.50.8). This was the beliefs of the people! If Prophet Muhammad was doing hearsay as you said, this is what he'll be doing: he'll be getting false information, and he will be transmitting it to the people. That's the first problem with what you're saying.", "The second problem with what you're saying is that the Prophet Muhammadﷺ, if he was doing what you're saying he was doing, another person will also have the same information, and we have no other sources, other than Islam, for this unique information in the Quran. So, if it was true that this was knowledge being circulated, we'll find it in different sources, but we don't!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Anonymous Atheist Attempts To Outsmart A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WC2nmWKjHVQ", ((1421, "23:41–24:33"), (1521, "25:21–25:48"), (1553, "25:53–26:50"), (1612, "26:52–27:04"),))
// U ML236:360-410 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("If he's getting it from the Jews and the Christians, then why is he refuting the beliefs of the Jews and the Christians? And why does he have information in Quran that is not found in the Books of Jews and Christians? Where did this information come from? And whoever was giving him this information, when the Prophetﷺ got authority, why didn't he come and say: this is my information, come, I'm the new leader?", "Allahﷻ says in the Quran (atTakwir81:22) وَمَا صَاحِبُكُم بِمَجْنُونٍۢ (And your Companion is not crazy). When Allahﷻ says صاحبكم (your Companion), why? He lived with them for 40 years. You know him; this is not some stranger. People lived there together in one community, in one society; they knew each other. So this صاحب of yours, this Companion of yours, is not crazy, because you lived with him. You know where he travelled, where he didn't travel. You saw him exiting and leaving the house and coming in. If he was getting this from somewhere, they'd have known that he's getting this from somewhere. Especially after he spoke about Prophethood and Messengerhood, people were all eyes on him, as they say. So if he went anywhere, left or right, they could have known straight away; they will clock he's going to this house, he's going to that location.", "A lot of the Christians mention Waraqa ibn Nawfal رحمه الله (may God have Mercy of him). Some of the scholars disagree: was he a Companion or not? They say رضي الله عنه (may [God] be satisfied with him), رحمه الله. And they say: OK, he got it from Waraqa ibn Nawfal, because after he got Revelation, he went to Waraqa ibn Nawfal. First, the person who took him to Waraqa ibn Nawfal (who was the cousin of Khadijahؓ, and was studying the Books of the Jews and the Christians) was Khadijahؓ! Was not the suggestion of the Prophetﷺ. When he went to Waraqa ibn Nawfal, he told him: \"this is the same angel that came to Moses\". Then he said to him: \"and if I was alive to see you, your people will kick you out\". Prophetﷺ said: \"you're going to kick me out?!\", because he is not thinking this. He was a honourable person from the tribe of Quraysh, respected; he didn't expect this. He said: \"yes, they will. There's no one who came with what you came with, except that he was kicked out.\" Then Waraqa ibn Nawfal encountered the Prophetﷺ maybe one more time, and he had passed away. So how can the Prophetﷺ be using him as a source of information for 23years later, when he has already passed away? And he was barely one or two encounters that happened? Makes no sense!", "So we say to them: we are welcoming any other alternative explanations. There's no other alternative explanations. And if every other possibility is void, there's only one: that what he said was the Truth. So that is the first thing that we can present to show that Islam is the Haqq حق (The Truth) from Allahﷻ.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Islam Unveiled: Compelling Evidence For The Truthfulness Of Islam | Chicago - USA | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUFsBco_CF0", ((1123, "18:43–19:05"), (1150, "19:10–19:58"), (1199, "19:59–21:03"), (1264, "21:04–21:22"),))
