#passage(("This guy, he quotes the same hadith three times, the same report, and he thinks it's three reports.", "Now here's what's interesting: the same hadith in another route says [Waraqa] used to write the gospel in Hebrew, non-Arabic. Did he write it in Arabic or in Hebrew? What these guys want to believe is that it was written in Arabic. The problem with that theory is that the Bible, the Gospels, they weren't available in Arabic at the time. It took at least one century for it to be translated into Arabic. It was translated through the orders of Harun al-Rashid, for example, so that's about a century and a half after the Prophet, peace be upon him. Why would they need to translate the gospel into Arabic if it was available, if [Waraqa] had already written the gospel in Arabic?", "Secondly, even if they were written in Arabic, the Prophet, peace be upon him, couldn't read Arabic. Thirdly, even if we assumed that the gospel was written in Arabic, the vast majority of the content that you find in the Quran about past nations is stuff that's [related] to the Old Testament, not the gospel, and we have reports saying that the Old Testament wasn't available in Arabic.",), "Farid Responds, “Ex-Muslim: Quran plagiarized Arabic Gospels!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m01Z06Eda0s", ((180, "3:00–3:17"), (197, "3:17–4:30"), (270, "4:30–5:06"),))
