#passage(("That's why you'll always see, not only historical, but even rational issues in the Bible. The Quran doesn't repeat, because these are interpolations, manipulations and corruptions of men. For instance, you have the idea of the original sin (Rom5:12). The Quran does not repeat that, because that is not rational and it's not from God. The idea that Adam was created perfect and he did not know right from wrong (Gen3:22): but how was he punished then after? When he was created he didn't know the knowledge of right or wrong. When he ate from the tree he learned. This information is not in the Quran.", "For instance, the Prophets of God were horrible individuals: worshipping other than God (1Kings11:4-13); adulterous (2Samuel:11); slept with his own daughter (Gen19:30-38); Abraham marrying his sister (Gen20:11-12). The list goes on! All of this, what we would call garbage because it's attributed to the Prophets of God, it's not in the Quran, because how would you come and learn from these people? God sends them as guidance for the mankind. Who's going to learn from someone who killed a man to get to sleep with his wife? (2Samuel:11) And the funny thing is that he killed a man to sleep with his wife and then he married her, and then he had Solomon from this woman that had adultery with him. At least we people, we have intellect, we have a mind. Please don't tell us these things that make us know for a fact this is unbelievable! If the Quran was copying, none of these things would make sense. It's impossible!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Unitarian Christian Questions The Similarities Between The Quran & The Bible! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t9EQwV9zMIE", ((819, "13:39–14:04"), (847, "14:07–15:04"),))

