#passage(("He mentioned the story of the infancy; he says that potentially existed around the 7th century. And he said that it's debated, there is no Arabic text. There was no Arabic text, for sure, 100%. It's not debated. So Prophet Muhammad couldn't have been reading these things and couldn't have been getting it from Arabs that are translating it and reading it. And the Quran, by the way, was revealed in 23 years, 13 years of it in Mecca, and there was no Jews and Christians there.", "A lot of Christians rely on Apocrypha text, by the way. Christians rely on Apocrypha text for historical reasons. For example, First Maccabees: they rely on it for many things to do with military and the numbers of people and stuff like that. They rely on certain texts to be early writings of the 1st century that are Apocrypha. Apocrypha texts, they're not in the canon, but they accept a lot of its historicity, like The Shepherd of Hermas, the Didache, about the traditions of the church, the Epistle of Barnabas, the First Epistle of Clement, and there's other things that Christians rely on which are Apocrypha texts, in which they would rely on to be historically accurate texts.", "Now, nobody can prove that the story in the Infancy Gospel did not exist or was not circulating in the 1st century. Nobody can prove that. He said that we know it's not from the 1st century. We don't have anything to show that it was, but you don't have anything to disprove that it was. We have things that would tie it to the 2nd century. We have nothing that disproves this idea that it was not circulating in the 1st century. And if it was circulating in the 1st century, 2nd century, whatever, how can you prove that this is not historically accurate, that it's actually an event that happened?", "And we know when the Quran was revealed for 23 years, Prophet Muhammad was not traveling anywhere. He was in Mecca and Medina when all of this revelation was coming down. So how is he able to recite all of this and say all of these things? And when he was not traveling to these regions, where is he collecting this information from? That is upon you now to provide proof for.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Wess Huff Claims The Quran Was Copied From The Bible | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hb-kHiXbGxI", ((935, "15:35–16:02"), (966, "16:06–16:46"), (1006, "16:46–17:15"), (1071, "17:51–18:10"),))
