#passage(("It's historically correct that the Pharaoh Ramses II claimed to be God, and it's a very significant detail that the Quran mentions and the Bible fails to mention, which shows that the Quran is not copying from the Bible or from the Apocrypha, because this is a historical event that took place, that we know today to be true, that the Quran records, while neither the Bible nor the Apocrypha records. Similarly, the idea of the people of Abraham worshipping the Moon and the Sun and Venus: this is something that the Quran records, that neither the Bible nor Apocrypha records, and is historically accurate. Which shows that the Quran is not taking from the Apocrypha, and it definitely not taking from the Bible, because these are all historical information that are not present in either of them. And if you were sincere, regardless of what happened to the sea and how the Pharaoh died, you'll have to answer this point and accept that this was not the source of whoever was authoring the Quran, which is God.", "We realize they're historically accurate after the death of prophet Muhammad, way after the death of Prophet Muhammad, just like some information about the Egyptians after discovering the Rosetta Stone in 1899 etc. or 1799, whatever it was. So that was way later after Prophet Muhammad. It was not discovered at the time of prophet Muhammad. It was not available.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Claims The Quran Is Historically Plagiarised! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ngAbQzpSvMw", ((1183, "19:43–20:35"), (1473, "24:33–25:02"),))
