#passage(("What is the percentage of these Gnostic stories in the Quran? How many of these stories are there? Quran is 6,000 verses. So we have a very minute portion of the Quran. Now, this very minute portion of the Quran allegedly correlates with apocryphal writings. Now, I can make a judgment (that's their claim) that proves that Quran is not from God, because there're stories that also exist in another historical source! Doesn't that sound like a ridiculous claim? The claim is that the Quran is not from God because there is 2% or 1% that exists in the Quran that also exists in other historical sources, but even the narrative is different. Therefore (now that's our argument) the Quran is not from God! How is that an argument? What I did is just took the argument and repeated it back to you, to see how ridiculous the arguments they make are. So these arguments are ridiculous, because you cannot jump into that conclusion with such a ridiculous claim. We reject your ridiculous claim.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Unitarian Christian Questions The Similarities Between The Quran & The Bible! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t9EQwV9zMIE", ((152, "2:32–4:01"),))
