#passage(("One man who existed 1,400 years ago, Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, he could not have brought this information on his own, and this information, most importantly, did not exist in previous scriptures: it's not in the Bible, it's not in the Greek mythology. Greeks, for example: what they believed about embryology! Everyone talks about how great Greeks were, but look at Galen and look at Aristotle: they will tell you that the baby was created from [menstrual] blood. Other Greeks, they said the first half of the baby is made, and then the second half in the belly. This was the people's beliefs at the time.", "If the Quran was not from God, if it was from a [mere] human being, it would also reflect the same knowledge in the culture. But the Quran disagrees with the culture, disagrees with the beliefs of the people, and introduces knowledge that nobody knew at the time, to show you that this must be coming from the creator of the heavens and the earth, the one who created everything.", "So we're saying: this universe that we're in, there must be something that brings it into existence. That something is beyond the knowledge that we have. So Prophet Muhammad made a claim that this Quran is coming from that creator. Now, how can we know that? If the knowledge in here reflects what that universe shows. Because if I made the universe, then I know it. So if I'm telling you about it, what I'm telling you will be the truth.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Muslim Students Get Introduced To The Miracles Of The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8oViMenjCIY", ((331, "5:31–6:31"), (393, "6:33–6:48"), (410, "6:50–7:12"),))
