#passage(("The Arabs (I'll give you some of the traditions): they would drink alcohol like water. They would bury their own daughters. Why? Because they believe daughters is a shame. If you have a daughter, they would bury their daughters alive: infanticide. They had superstitious things: they would think diseases spread by itself. This was the Arabs 1,400 years ago. They had no advancements in building. They were herders.", "You had the Roman and Persian Empire. This was the advancement, in the Roman and the [Sassanid] Empire and the [Byzantine] Empire. The Roman, Persian Empire didn't even care about them, because they were so insignificant. But when Islam came, they became a Muslim empire, and then the empire was all the way from China to Spain. That was because of Islam. The advancements came hundreds of years later: Muslims started reading and studying and applying that knowledge.", "1,400 years ago, when these verses was revealed, there was with the prophet, let's say, 10 followers, Muslims. The prophet was still preaching the message, and the people were persecuting him, trying to kill him. So who brought this information? You can be a scientist in biology, but you're not going to be a [scientist] in cosmology, embryology, hydrology, geology.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Buddhist Gets Defensive After A Muslim Highlights The Problems With Buddhism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cCyN0gL4kEI", ((3483, "58:03–58:41"), (3523, "58:43–59:10"), (3552, "59:12–59:34"),))
