#passage(("This Quran talks about the physical world, the physical reality: talks about the Universe, talks about Existence, and we're learning today, through our advancement in science, about the world. And if it was from this Bedouin Arab, it would have a lot of mistakes, because the knowledge of the people 1400 years ago about the world was wrong. Many people believed the world was flat, for example. Many people believed, like the Hindu Scripture, that the sun has seven horses pulling it (Rig Veda 1.50.8); the Earth has two bull horns that are holding it (Yajurveda 4-30). They had very ridiculous beliefs about the world, because this was their knowledge. So if this was coming from a man who wasn't a Prophet, you would have a lot of mistakes within it.", "But what we find is that the Quran is consistent with Reality. Rather, it's telling us things that we did not know about the reality, that we're learning today. For example, the Quran talks about the Universe and how the universe is expanding (Adhariyat51:47). In the 1900s, we learned that the universe is expanding. Now, the question would be: how would the Prophet Muhammad 1400 years ago know about this? And the people who knew this got the Nobel prize, while it is mentioned in the Quran all of this time.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “English Student Becomes Muslim! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vXu958o-hns", ((282, "4:42–5:25"), (330, "5:30–5:52"),))
