#passage(("Where is the stretch in the fact that the universe is expanding, and the Quran (adDhariyyat51:47) says the universe is expanding? It literally says expanding. What do you mean by \"interpretation\"? The universe is expanding in actuality, and the Quran says it's expanding. Where is the interpretation there?", "What you're doing right now is you're saying, \"It doesn't talk about the history of cosmology, of how it came to the point of expanding,\" disregarding the fact that it's giving you the conclusion that the people were not saying, that the Quran is saying that it's fact! Now, you're expecting the Quran to be a scientific cosmological book instead of a religious guidebook. The Quran is not a cosmological scientific book in which it will give you the history of the beginning of the universe until the point in which the universe is expanding, and start talking to you about redshifting and the fact that the wavelength of the galaxies is stretching, therefore you see the fabric of space itself stretching, and the equations to do with that. The Quran is not going to do that. If it did that, actually, it would be a never-ending infinite book that no one is going to read, and then there would be no point of it being a book of Guidance. The Quran is very small, and many people do not read regularly, so let alone if it was bigger than this.", "The Quran is going to come, speaking to the people of the time. There was no existence of general relativity. There were no equations in the way we're using equations today. And the Quran is going to come down to Bedouin Arabs, it's going to come down to people of that time with their level of knowledge, and it's going to talk to them about Einsteinian physics and cosmology, and give them general relativity, which is a term they don't understand, and give them equations of space and the cosmos and things they have no clue about, which is the exact opposite of wisdom!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Masked Philosophiser Attempts To Falsify Islam?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HeETj7W2uhw", ((1425, "23:45–24:10"), (1484, "24:44–25:56"), (1571, "26:11–26:54"),))
