#passage(("To drive this point home, it's worthy considering a thought experiment. This will show not only people like [Ridvan] are wrong about claiming science has disproved the Quran, but it will also refute those Muslims who claim that the Quran is a scientific miracle. Right now, as it stands, the consensus in physics is that the universe is expanding, and there are Muslims who claim this proves the Quran is a miracle, because the Quran also states that the universe is expanding: \"And the heaven we built it with might, and we are [lamusi'un]\" in surah 51, ayah number 47. The term [lamusi'un] is usually understood as meaning expanders: we are its expanders. The word heaven is taken to mean the universe and to be the object of the action of expanding, and thus it is claimed that this verse shows that the Quran has revealed that the universe is expanding.", "However, these Muslims are pinning one particular meaning to [lamusi'un] when it has a scope of meaning beyond this. [Musi'un] can also mean vast or ample, meaning God made the universe very big and spacious. The problem is that if this is a miracle, then only one meaning should be possible, that of the universe expanding. If it can mean expanding or large or both, it is no longer miraculous. That is one reason as to why this verse is not a scientific miracle in the scientific sense.", "And another reason is: how do these Muslims know that the science that tells us the universe is expanding is not going to change? Just because there is a consensus today doesn't mean it will hold forever. Imagine a [Ridvan] in 2070: he lives in a time when physics has gone through a paradigm shift, and the consensus is no longer that the universe is expanding, but rather that it is static and eternal. [Ridvan] 2070 will dig up the works from Muslims, including some scholars, of 2019, and will then claim that the Quran is wrong, as it claims that the universe is expanding when in fact it is not. We see here both [Ridvan] 2070 and some [Muslim] apologists are making the same mistake.",), "Farid Responds, “[DEBUNKED] The Science Mistakes of the Quran - Apostate Prophet”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6RTehKGfdCU", ((464, "7:44–8:35"), (517, "8:37–9:09"), (549, "9:09–9:55"),))
