#passage(("وَإِنَّا لَمُوسِعُونَ there is not a verb! (Adhariyyat51:47) وسّع/يوسّع أو أوسع: this is the verb. And وَإِنَّا لَمُوسِعُونَ is not a verb. This is جملة اسمية (Nominal sentence).", "So, the I'rab, the grammar of this specific part of the verse: first, the واو (Arabic letter \"waw\") used for وَإِنَّا لَمُوسِعُونَ; it's called واو الحال (Current waw). So it's something that is presently taking place. And where this واو is used, after it you have either جملة اسمية or جملة فعلية: you have either a sentence which is اسمية (nominal) or you have a sentence which is فعلية (verbal). This واو is for something that is presently taking place, and this جُملة (sentence), وَإِنَّا لَمُوسِعُونَ, this whole sentence is في مَحلّ نصبِ الحال; it is something that is happening right now. It is not something that has happened in the past. If Allahﷻ wanted to say that this is something in the past, it's no longer the case now, then Allah would say ولقد أوسعناها (and we have expanded it), or ولقد وسعناها (We expanded it), or وأوسعناها (We expanded it). He will use any of these other ways of describing. So this individual clearly does not understand the difference between present, between what is currently taking place, between past and continuous and present and future.", "He brought ابن كثير Ibn Kathir’s Tafsir (Exegesis of the Quran), which is exactly disproving his point! He's highlighted the wrong parts. Here it says: (Verily, we're able to extend the vastness of the space thereof). This is the Tafseer of Ibn Kathir that he is presenting and showing, trying to say that this is not talking about expanding it, and this is literally what the Tafseer is saying. If you open other basic Tafseer, they will say the same thing. For example, if you open السعدي Sa’di's Tafseer, he would say: \"وَإِنَّا لَمُوسِعُونَ في أرجائها وأنحائها، وإنا لموسعون أيضا على عبادنا، بالرزق\" (And we are expanding its parts, its surroundings, and we're also expanding provision upon Our servants). So these are two ways to understand, and you also understand وَإِنَّا لَمُوسِعُونَ (We have strength and power). All of these meanings can be taken from this جملة, this sentence وَإِنَّا لَمُوسِعُونَ. \"And We are expanding its parts and surroundings\", that which is above us, referring to this Cosmos: this is a perfectly valid explanation; it’s said in Tafseer Assa’di, and said in the same Tafseer that he has tried to use as evidence against what Muslims believe.", "Clearly, there's no understanding of the Arabic language. It is built on lies and, then, false premises of what the Sama’ means, then other false premises of the word كون as it was used in the past. On top of that, another false premise of not understanding the grammar of وَإِنَّا لَمُوسِعُونَ, thinking it's a past tense verb, when it's جملة: it's a sentence, it's not a verb.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| No Bible Contradictions? Following Mazhab? Mahdi Is Dajjal and more.. | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oDQFEUUc7kQ", ((358, "5:58–6:06"), (366, "6:06–7:07"), (458, "7:38–8:53"), (550, "9:10–9:26"),))
