#passage(("Everything he's presented, most of them are actually evidences for Islam and refutations of what he's saying, and completely misunderstanding of the language, or misunderstanding of science. And then he now tries to shrug off: \"Oh, look! I'm the educated atheist that knows how the science works today, and how the stars, and the moon, and how everything is happening, and you guys are still with this outdated knowledge.\" No! It is just that you are clearly not understanding the abc of what the Quran and the Hadith are talking about. For example, this verse: Allah says (adhDhariyat51:47) وَٱلسَّمَآءَ بَنَيْنَـٰهَا بِأَيْي۟دٍۢ وَإِنَّا لَمُوسِعُونَ (And the Sky above us, or whatever the universe above us, Allah has constructed with power). Where does it say there firmament around the Earth, or dome? Where does it say that? Why are you misrepresenting the verse of the Quran?", "This is the problem: he knows people are not going to go back to the references and read. He just says, \"Oh, it says this, it says that.\" No! But if you go back to the verse, you realise that he's lying! All it says is that: (Allah has constructed this universe with power), and then Allah says: وَإِنَّا لَمُوسِعُونَ (And we're expanding it). So that's evidence! It's giving you knowledge. Now that you talk about \"outdated\": no! It's knowledge that surpasses its time, 1400 years till today, and it will always surpass its time until the end of time.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| The Quran Has Multiple Errors?! Omar And The Pen & Paper Incident| Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_Q0bo07LFNs", ((1711, "28:31–29:13"), (1757, "29:17–29:59"),))
