#passage(("[Ridvan] is basing his whole attack on the Quran on the premise that the heavens are nothing, that they are void, that they are a vacuum. But this is simply wrong, because space itself can stretch and curve; there are even gravitational waves which can be experimentally measured. Only because you can't touch it or feel it doesn't mean it doesn't exist. The Quran merely says that the heavens [and] the earth, which is something that includes space, time and matter overall in the universe, was once joined in a single point and then later separated.", "[Ridvan] is arguing that the Quran suggests that the earth was [created] first. However, the Quran does not say this. The verse itself mentions that the sky was already in existence before the earth. What occurs after the creation of the earth was the formation of the seven heavens, and not the initial creation of the seven heavens.", "The universe actually had a stage in which there were primordial gas clouds that through gravity slowly formed into stars, galaxies and our solar system, including the already spherical earth. Smoke is a mixture of gases and particles, which in light to the scientific knowledge that we have is the right word to use.",), "Farid Responds, “[DEBUNKED] The Science Mistakes of the Quran - Apostate Prophet”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6RTehKGfdCU", ((1017, "16:57–17:31"), (1087, "18:07–18:27"), (1126, "18:46–19:05"),))
