#passage(("We have no way of estimating the size of one of these heavens. [Ridvan] arrives at the conclusion by quoting a hadith that says that each heaven is a distance of a 500 year march. However, it isn't a prophetic hadith, but rather a quote by [Ibn Mas'ud] radiyallahu anhu. The Quran does not state the distance of the nearest heaven, nor does the prophet Muhammad sallallahoalyhiwasallam. To keep it simple, the lowest heaven is not the atmosphere; it is the visible universe. The seven heavens are not simply galaxies, universes or the Earth's atmosphere.", "In regards to the seven Earth's, it seems like [Ridvan] assumes that they are Earth's like the earth that we live upon. There's no reason for this strange interpretation. All that we know of the seven Earth's is that they are below the ground that we live on, according to various hadiths of various ratings. We are unsure of how they look like, what they constitute, or at what level of the Earth's inner part they can be found. Modern science is unable to dig through every single part of the earth, especially taking into the account that we not even scratched the surface when it comes to digging up the planet.", "Also, scholars mentioned that the seven Earth's could be referring to a division into seven continents. What God defines as a continent or an earth can, logically speaking, be different as to what we define is an earth or a continent, depending on what we mean by this and depending on the social and environmental conditions that lead us to differing conclusions about the numbers of continents and layers of the earth.",), "Farid Responds, “[DEBUNKED] The Science Mistakes of the Quran - Apostate Prophet”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6RTehKGfdCU", ((625, "10:25–11:24"), (709, "11:49–12:24"), (744, "12:24–12:47"),))
