#passage(("[Ridvan] claims that the sky is not some type of ceiling above us and that it can't fall down into the earth. Let's go to a scientific article called What if the sky fell: \"Paradoxically, this is no airy affair. All the oxygen, nitrogen, and other stuff in Earth's atmosphere has a whooping combined mass of 5 quadrillion tons. So a falling sky would mean that nearly 10 tons of molecules, roughly the heft of a school bus, would drop on every square meter of Earth's surface. Pancakes, in other words.\"", "First of all, the word sky in Arabic can mean different things. It can mean literally the roof of a house. It can mean that which is above you, that which encompasses all things in creation. So the sky could be simply the atmosphere above us that, according to a scientific article, can actually fall on us. It can be condensed onto us and crushed onto us.", "Another thing is the sky could be referring to the known universe, and the known universe, although it doesn't have edges, has limits. It can be condensed into a singular point, let alone the earth. It is a known fact in science that the phenomena of the big crunch is possible; in other words, the whole universe collapsing back into a singular point, as it was a singular point, according to most scientists, in the beginning. So for it to collapse on the earth is also possible, because the earth is even bigger than a singular point.",), "Farid Responds, “[DEBUNKED] Allah holds the Sky? - Apostate Prophet”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A7pf0f3Wj1g", ((97, "1:37–2:15"), (139, "2:19–2:45"), (165, "2:45–3:17"),))
