#passage(("It's quite disingenuous when I look at sometimes how these people look at these verses of the Quran and misinterpret them. In the Chapter that he's mentioning, Chapter:21, verse:33, Allah says: وَهُوَ ٱلَّذِی خَلَقَ ٱلَّیۡلَ وَٱلنَّهَارَ (He's the One Who created day and night) وَٱلشَّمۡسَ وَٱلۡقَمَرَۖ (Sun and Moon). So you have two different ones now: created Day and Night, and created Sun and Moon. And then Allah says كُلࣱّ (each of them – the Sun and Moon) فِی فَلَكࣲ یَسۡبَحُونَ (they're orbiting). Each of them, the Sun and the Moon, are orbiting.", "Now, he makes the claim: they don't orbit around the Earth. Where is the description at all in this verse anywhere? Where is the word \"earth\" mentioned? Where does it mention anywhere here orbiting around the Earth? All it says is that (Allah Created also the Day and Night and He created the Sun and the Moon). So, these are two separate sentences. And the واو in the Arabic language, the letter (waw), is to separate between the things. And then, he claims and says: Oh! there is a Scientific error in the Quran. No! there's no scientific error in the Quran.", "Now, Allah also mentions the same thing in chapter:39, verse:5 of the Quran (azZumar), where He mentions: وَسَخَّرَ ٱلشَّمۡسَ وَٱلۡقَمَرَۖ (And He guided–), now specifically talking about the Moon and the Sun. And then Allah says: كُلࣱّ (Each of them) -again- (Each of them are also orbiting). So, Allah specifically talks about how the Sun is orbiting.", "And this knowledge we didn't have 50-60 years ago. We had a completely different system of the galaxy and sun and stars and moon. And we had this incorrect belief that was taught in the books 60-70 years ago, that the sun doesn't have an orbit, doesn't move! So, this verse is actually a sign, it's an evidence! And most of these verses that you're bringing, you're trying to make a claim that they are mistakes, they're all evidences! Splitting of the moon is an evidence of the veracity and the Truthfulness of Islam.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| The Quran Has Multiple Errors?! Omar And The Pen & Paper Incident| Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_Q0bo07LFNs", ((641, "10:41–11:12"), (674, "11:14–11:50"), (712, "11:52–12:09"), (733, "12:13–12:41"),))
