#passage(("He claims here, the Quran is saying \"the Earth\"; when he says \"the Earth\", he refers to the sphere of the celestial body of what we call the planet Earth. Now, the Quran is not describing that. All of the verses that he mentioned in the Quran mentions the same word: الأرض. For example, Allah says (Nuh71:19) جَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلْأَرْضَ بِسَاطًۭا (Allah, He made for you الأرض). Now what does this word الأرض mean, actually, in language? How do we understand this verse? Now, الأرض in the Quran and in the language of the Arabs, and in the understanding of every person who speaks language, the word الأرض in the Arabic language refers to \"land\", not necessarily specifically the celestial huge body, what we refer to as Earth. Now, you have to present to us: where does the Quran talk about the whole celestial body, clearly, and then says that the whole celestial body is flat? Which you will find nowhere in the Quran.", "But Allah is talking about us now. He made for us this land, الأرض. He's made it for us, spread out. Is this false or true? When you go walking right now, is that أرض spread out for you? Or do you turn over like a ball and rotate? No! It's spread out for you. So, Allah is referring to the perception that you have as a human being. And Allah, in many many places in the Quran, uses the same term الأرض. Allah for example says (alBaqara2:168) كُلُوا۟ مِمَّا فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ حَلَـٰلًۭا طَيِّبًۭا (Eat from that which is in the الأرض): it refers to the land. Allah says (alBaqara2:60) وَلَا تَعْثَوْا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ (Do not go in the land causing corruption). It's talking about the land.", "Now, what's very interesting is also that Allahﷻ says in the Quran, in chapter:39 (azZumar), verse:5: یُكَوِّرُ ٱلَّیۡلَ عَلَى ٱلنَّهَارِ وَیُكَوِّرُ ٱلنَّهَارَ عَلَى ٱلَّیۡلِۖ. So, (Allah circles..): the word يُكَوِّرُ comes from the Arabic word كُرة (Ball). So, Allah says (He circles the night over the day and He circles the day over the night), and that can only happen if the Earth is round, in which you can go with the night and the day in a circular motion. Is this my understanding? No! This is the understanding way before NASA existed, way before satellites, way before we could see the shape of the Earth. You have Shaykh alIslam Ibn Taymiyyah, and you have many many Scholars in Islam. You have Ibn Hazm, people who lived in Andalusia, people who lived (we're talking about 400, 500 or 600 years back from today) who reported the consensus of Muslim scholars that the Earth is round. And what did they use as evidence? They used this verse! And they said: from this verse we come to the understanding that the Earth is round. And also Ibn Hazm says: \"I have not known any person, any scholar of knowledge that goes against this opinion.\"", "And bear in mind: when the Muslims believed that, the overwhelming majority of people used to believe it's flat! So Muslims stood on that opinion because the Quran says so. And it said against what? \"Science\" and what people thought at the time. But the Quran was correct, and today we know the Quran is correct.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| The Quran Has Multiple Errors?! Omar And The Pen & Paper Incident| Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_Q0bo07LFNs", ((985, "16:25–17:14"), (1038, "17:18–17:58"), (1086, "18:06–19:12"), (1175, "19:35–19:51"),))
