#passage(("One thing to destroy this entire ridiculous narrative is, first: we already showed the hypocrisy, where they have all the copies of themselves, whether it is the Epic of Gilgamesh, whether it is the New Testament copying the Old Testament, whether it is the pagan traditions. But the most important thing is this: if it's true that the Quran is copying from the previous scriptures and Prophet Muhammad is copying from the previous scriptures, then it would copy what it says word for word. But we have historical errors in the Bible that the Quran corrects.", "One famous one is the story of Joseph. The leader at the time of Joseph in the Bible is called Pharaoh. And the leader at the time of Moses is called Pharaoh. But we know in Egyptology that this is false. We know there's historical Egyptian periods. We have the early kingdom or first kingdom, and middle kingdom, and the end kingdom, last kingdoms. We have all of these different differentiations between the historical periods in Egyptology, in Egyptian history: the New Kingdom, the middle intermediate kingdom and the middle kingdom. So, Joseph was around the middle kingdom or in the middle intermediate kingdom. And Moses was in the New Kingdom.", "And the term Pharaoh was not used, because it was the period of the Hyksos. At the time of Joseph, it was the period of the Hyksos. It was a king. It was not a Pharaoh. The term Pharaoh was not used for the leader. It was later on historically used for the leader. It was used for the palace first, and then they started using it for the leader in the new kingdom, at the time of Moses. So the Bible is making historical error there, calling the leader at the time of Joseph a pharaoh.", "Now the Quran corrects that. The Quran, if he's copying from the Bible, it would call the leader at the time of Joseph and the leader at the time of Moses, they would call both of them pharaoh, but it doesn't. It calls the leader at the time of Joseph a king, and it calls the leader at the time of Moses a pharaoh. Showing you that it's not copying anything. It's actually correcting that false information in these scripts in the Bible.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Wess Huff Claims The Quran Was Copied From The Bible | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hb-kHiXbGxI", ((1092, "18:12–18:49"), (1131, "18:51–19:33"), (1174, "19:34–20:04"), (1206, "20:06–20:27"),))
