#passage(("You have information in the Quran that is not even in the Bible to begin with. It's not in the Bible and it's not in apocryphal text. So tell us, where is it from? There is many stories, many instances. I'll give you an example. You have Abraham, where the Quran has this record in Surah An'am. It has this entire dialogue between Abraham and his people. And it's showing you that they used to worship a planet. They used to worship the sun and they used to worship the moon. We don't see this in apocrypha and we don't see this in the Bible.", "However, we discovered a historical artifact: in Ur, you have a temple called Ziggurat of Ur. And Sumerian language was a dead language anyways; Prophet Muhammad couldn't have read it. But the temple was also buried under the sand. We discovered there is [an] artifact in it that says that the people at that time used to worship triad: Ishtar, the goddess of Venus, a planet, and the god of sun, Shamash, and the goddess of moon, Nanna. So the Quran is highlighting this historical reality that we are discovering recently, which doesn't exist in the Bible or apocrypha, about historical reality at the time of Abraham. Where did the Prophet Muhammad bring in this information from, if he was, as you claim, copying these stories? And I can give more evidences. Now it's upon you to demonstrate where is Prophet Muhammad bringing this information from. Produce your proof. Where is he getting this information from, if it didn't exist in these places and it didn't exist in what you're claiming Prophet Muhammad is copying from?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Wess Huff Claims The Quran Was Copied From The Bible | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hb-kHiXbGxI", ((1229, "20:29–21:10"), (1270, "21:10–22:09"),))
