#passage(("There are orientalists that disagree with [Puin's] assessment in regards to the Quran. What is wrong with these orientalists? Were they lying about the Quran making sense? Are they delusional? Well, maybe, because I can't think of a good reason for orientalists to claim that the Quran makes sense apart from it actually making sense. So why can't someone say something like: \"I have no idea what is going on here, so I'm going to say that this is incomprehensible, but instead of the fault being with me, let's pretend that I am an expert\"?", "Ever heard of the alleged expert that says that the Quran is beautiful and unique and that there was no precedent for it in the earlier literature of the ancient Arabs? \"Its effusion from the tongue of an illiterate man with no education, let alone literary training, is a phenomenon which in this respect can justifiably be described as a miracle.\" He also praises some specific chapters as a shining example of prophetic eloquence. And [guess] who this is referring to? Yes, it's [Ali], your own source, the person that you refer to as an expert. Just to be clear, [Ali] does not believe that the Quran in itself is a miracle of eloquence; however, these statements clearly conflict with what David is trying to present to his audience. So do you agree, David? Do you believe that Ali's assessment is correct? Do you believe that he's an expert? I personally don't, by the way. But do you agree with his claims? Is he only an expert when it suits you?",), "Farid Responds, “David Wood Challenged me to Refute this Video”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o6MinzBhq5o", ((180, "3:00–3:42"), (273, "4:33–5:35"),))
