#passage(("If the Quran is supposed to be Guidance, part of that Quran tells you to go to the people of knowledge (Annahl16:43), and the example of these Prophet and companions will be an explanation for you to understand how to live by this book. So, part of the Quran directs you to those people of knowledge, because it's also directing you by Guidance, that not everyone has the same level of understanding. Someone might take the Quran and understand it very well; someone might understand it less. [He] would need someone to help him, give him a little bit of expounding, teach him a little bit. That doesn't mean it's confusing. Expounding upon something, which is wise, does not necessitate that the statement that was made was confusing or incorrect.", "The Prophet is the example, as the Quran says, for us. For example, Allah says لَّقَدْ كَانَ لَكُمْ فِي رَسُولِ اللَّهِ أُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ لِّمَن كَانَ يَرْجُو اللَّهَ وَالْيَوْمَ الْآخِرَ (Alahzab33:21) (Whoever wishes goodness on the last day, had an example in the Prophet). So we look at the life of the Prophet, and how he lived his life. Allah tells us about his Companions and those who followed them (Attawba9:100). Not just his Companions, but we have التابعون وأتباع التابعين (The generations, a couple of generations that came after), because the Prophet told us that: \"The best of generation is my generation, and those who come after them, then the ones who come after them.\" And this is for example what you would see Sheikh Alislam Ibn Taymiyyah in this voluminous work he's doing: he's referring to these people, the Companions of the Prophet who learned directly from him, because he was the example, or the students who took from them, or the students of the students who took from them.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Confronts Muslim On The Clarity Of The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ozeX5ELYDh0", ((520, "8:40–9:13"), (564, "9:24–10:07"),))
