#passage(("If you are sincere then you can find guidance eventually, إن شاء الله. But if you just try to ignore the clear verses then you'll always be misguided.", "Allah says in the Quran something beautiful in chapter 3 of the Quran, verse 7. It is very important, it deals with the Christians. Allah says فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ زَيْغٌ, those who have a disease in their hearts, فَيَتَّبِعُونَ مَا تَشَابَهَ مِنْهُ, they follow the ambiguous verses that have more than one meaning and they ignore the clear verses, seeking to cause corruption. This is the principle of people of deviation, the people of falsehood: they build their belief on the implicit verses. Another principle of the people of deviation is that they believe something, then look in the text to what supports their belief. They don't look at the text and derive their belief from the text; they believe first, and then they look in the text to justify what they believe. And we've got deviant groups in the Islamic community that do the same. I'm not even saying just Christians do that, because this verse here is in the Quran, so it's addressing the Muslims as well as teaching them.", "There is not a single verse that is explicit that supports your creed, your beliefs. There's only explicit verses that destroy your belief, like Jesus saying he \"does not know\", and God is all knowing. You cannot be God and you do not know. Or finding a verse that says \"the father is the only true god\", which completely destroys the concept of the Trinity, and these are the explicit verses. So the explicit verses actually go against your faith rather than supporting you. So you should be sincere and should then accept: \"What he's saying actually makes sense here. I need to look into this, because there's nothing in my Scripture that actually supports what I believe. Why do I actually believe what I believe, when the scripture does not support?\" That's what a sincere person would do.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Convert Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s7wX-huScq0", ((897, "14:57–15:01"), (907, "15:07–16:14"), (985, "16:25–17:03"),))
