#passage(("We say usually that in language, letters do not have meaning, only words have meaning. So, tell me the meaning of M or L or O or X: you cannot tell me a meaning of a letter. A letter does not have a meaning; what has a meaning is a word that is combined with different letters.", "In the beginning of the chapter there are three letters there, but we don't read them as a word. If we read them as a word, it will be ألم (Alam), and this exists in other parts of the Quran where we read them as a word, and they have a meaning, for example سورة الفيل (Surat Alfeel: Elephant Chapter) (105:1). Allah says: أَلَمۡ تَرَ كَیۡفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِأَصۡحَـٰبِ ٱلۡفِیلِ (Didn't you see what your Lord did to the People of the Elephant). So \"Alam\" there becomes \"didn't you\", becomes a word that has a meaning. But in the beginning of the chapters we read them as letters: Alif, Laam, Meem. These are 3 letters; we read them letter, letter, letter, which means that these are letters, and letters do not have meaning. Therefore (Alif, Laam, Meem) does not have a meaning.", "But there's a wisdom behind Allah putting them in the Quran. Why did Allah use them in the Quran? It is because you will always see after using these letters, like الٓمٓ (Alif, Laam, Meem) (Albaqara2:1), كۤهیعۤصۤ (Kaaf, Haa, Ya, 'Ayn, Saad) (Mariam19:1), الٓرۚ (Alif, Laam, Raa) (Yusuf12:1): all of these letters that Allah puts in the beginning, Allah usually in most cases will speak about the Quran in the next verse. So: الۤمۤ ۝ ذَ ٰ⁠لِكَ ٱلۡكِتَـٰبُ (Alif Laam Meem. This is the Book) (Albaqara2:1-2): Allah will speak about the Quran. So why are they there? It is because it's a challenge for the Arabs. The Arabs were challenged to bring something like the Quran. That was a challenge to the Arabs because the Quran came in the eloquent Arabic language, and the Arabs at the time of the Prophetﷺ, this was their speciality. So Allah brought a Revelation that is in the field of their speciality to challenge them, because you can say \"oh, I don't know what this is\", but if it's your field you know what is miraculous and what is not. So Allah revealed the Quran in the Arabic language and challenged them to bring something like it. Then Allah is revealing these Arabic letters and saying: look, this is your language (Alif, Laam, Meem), this is your letters, the same Arabic letters that you use; why aren't you able to bring something like it? This Book no one can imitate or bring anything like! So Allah put these letters, as many of the scholars said, as a challenge for them, saying to them: use them and bring something like the Quran, if you claim that it is false and it is not truly from the Creator.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Popular Youtuber Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S7bA8bsNs20", ((537, "8:57–9:07"), (551, "9:11–9:42"), (585, "9:45–10:53"),))
