#passage(("Allah says that if you disagree over anything, there has to be evidential text to prove. You have to go to the Quran or Hadith, either \"the Prophet says\" or \"Allah says\", in order for us to follow what you say. Now, with the Bible, some can say, \"I understand it that way\" and that's it. You cannot go back to the beliefs of, for example, the followers of Jesus, or you go back to Jesus himself practising. You don't have that, and you don't have the Bible saying that this is how you solve your disagreements. So, the Quran gives you clear principles on what to do when there is any disagreement. That solves these disagreements and leads you to guidance in the end.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Lady Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2EcJiOmZI44", ((1200, "20:00–20:29"),))
