#passage(("When you say \"for me\", you realize the Quran is objective religious text. When I take you back, I put you in a time machine 1,400 years ago, is it going to mean something different? No. \"Three, the fourth is a dog\" is going to mean the same thing.", "Now, the Quran is not a scripture that came to us in a vacuum, meaning we did not wake up one day and we look at the sky and the Quran was descending. When the Quran came down, it came upon the messenger of God.", "First, there's clear verses that doesn't need interpretation. But for other verses that can have multiple interpretations, I cannot come and say \"for me\". The idea \"for me\" doesn't apply. Why? Because we already have a criteria of how to understand the scripture. That criteria will be the first generation of Muslims, a prophet and his companions. When I say it's objective religious text, meaning the statements of [Prophetﷺ] are objective text, the Quran is objective text.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Hijabi Woman Confronts Muslim On The Hijab Not Being In The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BzefH8uharg", ((32, "0:32–1:15"), (126, "2:06–2:22"), (169, "2:49–4:09"),))
