#passage(("I'll tell you how atTabari does his Tafsir. AtTabari has one of two ways he will do something. So first, Abu Ja'far, who is ibn Jarir atTabari (that's his full name), when he does an interpretation of a verse of the Quran, he either first says his interpretation of the verse (when I say \"his interpretation\", meaning what he collected from the scholars). So he goes on and mentions parts of the verse, part by part, and then he goes on to explain what it means. So that's one way. Or he will do that first sometimes, and then will go into difference of views. So he will say: some people said \"this\" means \"this\", some people said \"this\" means \"that\". And then he will go on after that mentioning narrations. Narrations from who? From the تابِعين (Tabi'in), meaning the students of the Companions of The Prophet, or the Companions of The Prophet directly. So he will go on and say, for example, \"Qatada said..\", \"Mujahid said..\", \"X narrates from Z, from this person, that Qatada said that it means this\". So he will say, \"OK, people said it means that\", and then he will go on giving you a list of narrations. Then he will say, \"Other people said this\", and he'll give you a list of narrations. So either he will give you his interpretation first, and does that, or he will do that first, and then in the end tell you: \"and I think the best interpretation is X\", or \"the best interpretation is Y\".", "Or some verses would be super clear that they don't really need interpretation, like for example (Say Allah is One) (alikhlas112:1). He is not going to really need to tell you that \"People said this, means this\". It doesn't really require that. Some things would be very clear, so he will just explain the meaning, and that's it. So that's how Tafsir atTabari works, and that's why it's not translated: It's massive, number 1. Number 2, it is in the classical standard Arabic; therefore it's not easy for someone to come, just a random person, to come and translate the book.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “King James Christian Challenges Muslim On Bible Preservation! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eSGX_1-ukxw", ((460, "7:40–8:51"), (532, "8:52–9:19"),))
