#passage(("When Allahﷻ says (Alikhlas112:1) قُلۡ هُوَ ٱللَّهُ أَحَدٌ (Say \"He is Allah, One ˹and Indivisible˺), Qul is to me and you, not only to Prophet Muhammedﷺ. But Qul to who? Muslims already believe Allah is أَحَدٌ (Ahad: One and Indivisible). You're going to say to people who don't believe Allahﷻ is Ahad. Qul: testify. فَٱصۡدَعۡ بِمَا تُؤۡمَرُ (So proclaim what you have been commanded) (Alhijr15:94): صدع is like loud voice, loud noise, make it clear, apparent, the Message that you're giving. وَقُلِ ٱلۡحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّكُمۡۖ (And say \"˹This is˺ the Truth from your Lord) (Alkahf18:29).", "قُلۡ یَـٰۤأَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَـٰبِ (Say, \"O People of the Book!) (Alimran3:64): Qul again! But here it's clear: Ahl Alkitab (People of the Book i.e. Jews and Christians). So, no one can say it's Qul about someone else. قُلۡ یَـٰۤأَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَـٰبِ تَعَالَوۡا۟ إِلَىٰ كَلِمَةࣲ سَوَاۤءِۭ بَیۡنَنَا وَبَیۡنَكُمۡ أَلَّا نَعۡبُدَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَ (Come to a common term between us and you that we worship Allah alone). So Allah is telling you here: go say to the people of the Scriptures. And Allah He says قُلْ يَا أَهْلَ الْكِتَابِ لَا تَغْلُوا فِي دِينِكُمْ (Say Ô People of Scripture, do not transgress in your religion) (Almaida5:77), وَلَا تَقُولُوا۟ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡحَقَّۚ (and do not say except the Truth about Allah) (Annissa4:171). And Allah says to them themselves (Annisaa4:171): وَلَا تَقُولُوا۟ ثَلَـٰثَةٌۚ (And do not say Three (Trinity)). So all of these verses are explicit and clear.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Reason Some \"Muslims\" Celebrate Christmas! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ti1oJEBzsOs", ((473, "7:53–8:27"), (513, "8:33–9:09"),))
