#passage(("The second thing he says is that there's a word in the Arabic language for Universe, الكَون (alkawn). Alkawn الكون (used today in modern Arabic to refer to existence, cause it comes from كان/يكون) is referring to everything that exists. There was never usage of that word in the previous times in that way. This is a new modern way of using this term. If you go to classical dictionaries, open Lisan al'Arab and look at the word alKawn, you're never going to see Lisan al'Arab telling you alKawn means the Universe or everything in existence. This is a new usage of the word, and this 21st century Arab is a prime example of that. He speaks modern Arabic, 21st century, and he thinks he understands the Arabic of the Quran.", "When you look at the Quran in other places, does the Quran ever use the word الكَون? Does the Prophetﷺ ever use the word الكون? Do the Sahaba (Companions) use the word الكَون to mean the Universe? You're not going to find that word, because the Arabs did not use that word. You're not going to find it in the pre-Islamic poetry, because that usage that you're using today, the modern usage of the Arabic language, was not used in that way at that time.", "I'm not surprised that he is not a Muslim, because the Arabs that properly understand the Arabic language will see the miraculous nature of the Quran, and they will definitely become Muslims. You have to be someone who's illiterate when it comes to the Arabic language to criticise the Arabic language from a linguistic standpoint, and this person clearly does not understand the Arabic language, does not understand إعراب (i'rab: Parsing), which is how the Arabic grammar works.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| No Bible Contradictions? Following Mazhab? Mahdi Is Dajjal and more.. | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oDQFEUUc7kQ", ((228, "3:48–4:23"), (269, "4:29–4:45"), (328, "5:28–5:47"),))
