#passage(("Who's that person that Allah said سَأُصْلِيهِ سَقَر? There's a specific person! That's why you cannot take the Quran out of context. Allahﷻ is speaking about a specific person who, after knowing that the Prophet Muhammadﷺ is a Messenger of God and knowing that The Quran is The Truth, he chose to disbelief and he chose to disobey Allahﷻ specifically.", "If you read Surat Al-Muddaththir from the beginning, you will see that Allahﷻ is speaking about that individual (Quran74:23-11): ذَرْنِي وَمَنْ خَلَقْتُ وَحِيدًا * وَجَعَلْتُ لَهُ مَالًا مَّمْدُودًا * وَبَنِينَ شُهُودًا * وَمَهَّدتُّ لَهُ تَمْهِيدًا * ثُمَّ يَطْمَعُ أَنْ أَزِيدَ * كَلَّا ۖ إِنَّهُ كَانَ لِآيَاتِنَا عَنِيدًا * سَأُرْهِقُهُ صَعُودًا * إِنَّهُ فَكَّرَ وَقَدَّرَ * فَقُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَ * ثُمَّ قُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَ * ثُمَّ نَظَرَ * ثُمَّ عَبَسَ وَبَسَرَ * ثُمَّ أَدْبَرَ وَاسْتَكْبَرَ. So Allah in all of that is talking about a specific individual; he is called Alwaleed Bin Almugheera, by the way. So this verse is revealed specifically about that specific individual; you cannot then completely apply to every disbeliever on Earth.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Tunisian Girl Questions Muslim On Women's Rights! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l68vK6nDhbA", ((688, "11:28–11:55"), (721, "12:01–12:34"),))
