#passage(("Surat alImran, Verse:81, the covenant of the Prophets. Allah doesn't say a specific Prophet, but Allah tells all the Prophets: if a Prophet comes to you, that you are going to support him, that you're going to believe in him, that you're going to accept him. That is the covenant that was taken upon all these Prophets. And the Verse says not in specific term about a specific individual, but it says \"if\": if came to you a Messenger, that you're going to support him, etc. Of course, there are مُفَسِّرون (mufassiroon), there are exegetes, Muslim exegetes who say that this is, for example, about the Prophet Muhammadﷺ. But in reality, this Verse, if you're talking about the Verse itself, just the wording of the Verse, it does not necessarily specifically mention a specific individual, but it's a general Verse as a covenant for the Prophets. And the Messengers accepted that covenant.", "Allahﷻ says in the Quran that Allah is the witness over everything, so I have no problem with this Verse. Allah says in the Quran (alHajj22:17) إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ شَهِيدٌ (Allah is a witness over everything). So yes, of course, when that Messenger comes to those other Messengers, Allah is going to be a Witness, because Allah is a Witness over everything.", "You quoted the Verse of the Quran and then you introduced your Book about the Secret Treasury, or whatever term you want to use for that Book, this name which is nowhere in the Quran! And you use the Verse, which doesn't mention anything about Sacred Treasury, it doesn't mention anything about the man or the Prophet or whoever you believe in, and then somehow you want to convince us that this Verse is about him, even though it mentions nothing to do with him or anything about the Sacred Treasury. It's like you're saying the sky is blue, therefore, there is milk in my fridge! You're missing the connection between the two information.", "Allahﷻ says in the Quran: وَإِذۡ أَخَذَ ٱللَّهُ مِیثَـٰقَ ٱلنَّبِیِّـۧنَ, when Allah took that covenant, oath, (from the Prophets), لَمَاۤ ءَاتَیۡتُكُم مِّن كِتَـٰبࣲ وَحِكۡمَةࣲ (That I gave you): Allah gave them (Book and wisdom). He gave them revelation, He gave them wisdom, he gave them Prophethood. ثُمَّ جَاۤءَكُمۡ رَسُولࣱ مُّصَدِّقࣱ لِّمَا مَعَكُمۡ لَتُؤۡمِنُنَّ بِهِۦ وَلَتَنصُرُنَّهُۥۚ (Then came to you a Messenger confirming that which you have). So now this covenant is specifically for the Messengers. There is a Messenger that exists; that Messenger comes to him another Messenger from Allah confirming that which he has. Then Allah is saying to that Messenger: are you going to believe in that Messenger too, and support him, aid him? Then the Messengers say to Allah: yes, we will; we take the oath, we take that covenant. Then Allah is saying: since you took that covenant, I'm Witness upon you, meaning that when it comes to you that other Messenger, to you who are a Messenger, I'm witness to you, if you're keeping your covenant or if you're not keeping your covenant. So the Verse of the Quran, which is explicitly clear, very explicit, it's talking about a Messenger of God and another Messenger of God coming to a Messenger of God. Now, somehow you took that Verse, which talks about Prophets and Messengers in the past, because there is no more Prophets and Messengers, and you're trying to convince us that somehow this talks about the Sacred Treasury and some new guy that came out of nowhere.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sacred Treasurey Follower Challenges Muslim On The Final Revelation! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IwY1FORIiaU", ((705, "11:45–12:44"), (777, "12:57–13:13"), (909, "15:09–16:09"), (976, "16:16–17:47"),))
