#passage(("The terms you used are not what the Quran is using. You say clean and unclean; let's see where the Quran says that he made certain things clean that were unclean. This terminology I don't believe is in the Quran; perhaps there's something I'm missing! English words have a meaning as well, clean and unclean; I know what they mean in Arabic, and this term is not used there.", "Permissible is different: وَلِأُحِلَّ لَكُم بَعْضَ ٱلَّذِى حُرِّمَ عَلَيْكُمْ ۚ (al'Imran3:50), “So that I can make certain things permissible for you\", or \"some of the things that were made impermissible for you permissible”. Clean and unclean is a complete different thing, that could refer to, I don't know, to Foods or specific other things. So, I'm very particular with my words, and I'm very particular with the Quran even more, like x100 times, what exactly it says, because we don't need misrepresentations of what it says, and then arguments are built on misrepresentations often times.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Jew Claims Rational Problems With Islam?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8isq12mnPYs", ((1358, "22:38–23:03"), (1425, "23:45–24:17"),))
