#passage(("(Annahl16:42) There's two understandings that can be understood from this verse. One of them: the verse says “فَاسْأَلُوا أَهْلَ الذِّكْرِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ” (Ask the people of الذّكْرِ Dhikr), so I'm giving you that literal translation now, إِنْ كُنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ (if you do not know). Now, the people of Dhikr here can be one of two things. It can be the people of knowledge, people of the Quran and Sunnah (Prophetic Traditions), because the word in the Quran is used for the Quran itself, and it's used for the Sunnah as well, it's used for the Hadith (Prophetic Sayings). So when it says ask the people of Dhikr, it refers to the scholars, the people of the Quran and Sunnah. So that's one understanding.", "Another understanding is that Dhikr can refer to previous Scriptures. So here this verse then would mean: ask the people of the previous scriptures if you do not know. What would you ask the people of the previous scriptures about? We would ask them about the Prophets and Messengers, because this verse in the beginning is telling you that Allahﷻ sent Prophets and Messengers in the past. You will go to the Jews and Christians and ask them: did you have Prophets and Messengers, like a person called David, a person called Solomon? Did you have these Prophets and Messengers or no? So if you do not know, you can ask the people of the Scriptures, and they will confirm for you that there were previous Messengers that were sent, asking to worship one God alone, just like the Quran says.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sister Cries After Realising Islam Is The Truth! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PtJpInP1jl8", ((58, "0:58–2:11"), (133, "2:13–2:39"),))
