#passage(("The reason because [Musa] was extremely in a state of anger, in which he was not 100% noticing what he's doing with everyone around him. It's not 100% the same state as someone who's not angry. Because the minute he left them, he came back, he found them worshipping the [calf] straight. He said: I hasten to my Lord to worship him; he comes back, he finds these people are worshiping, and then he put the accountability on his brother; his brother was a prophet of God, [Harun]. He said: how is this happening when you're here? How is this happening? And then, because of the state of anger, he took his beard, etc. But that's not something that would happen all the time, or we should be doing.", "And this is a situation of something to do with the religion of Allah, of people who went to the extent of committing [disbelief], worshiping other than Allah. So this is a different scenario: people did a major thing, the biggest [sin] they could do, [shirk], and someone was supposed to be responsible, and then you're trying to hold him accountable in that way for that event that took place. So the prophets of God are the best of people, but they're humans, so there will be certain situation, and there will be a state of anger, etc.; something might happen; it's not to be applicable in all situations and scenarios.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Eddie @TheDeenShowTV Interviews The Muslim Lantern | Masjid Dar Al-Qur'an | Chicago - USA”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sLfJyJGj_eg", ((5131, "1:25:31–1:26:17"), (5180, "1:26:20–1:26:59"),))
