#passage(("This idea that Allahﷻ sent Angel Gabriel to Pharaoh when he was dying, Ramses the 2nd, when he was dying, telling him that if you accept Islam now, I will forgive you: that's not authentic; there's nothing in the Quran or Sunnah that says that. The Quran actually clearly says the problem with Pharaoh: what he did is that Pharaoh claimed to be God! He just did Shirk, he just claimed to be God himself. He said: \"فَقَالَ أَنَا رَبُّكُمُ الْأَعْلَىٰ\" (I'm your lord the Most-High) (Quran79:24). And then all his life, even though he was shown signs, and Allah mentions in the Quran that He's shown many many signs, the signs that Moses showed him when he came to him, he showed him many signs that Allah mentions in the Quran, that are also mentioned in the Bible, but he still persisted in his disbelief, and he called Moses a liar, and he was trying to kill Musa 'Alayhi salam (peace be upon him) and his people, until Musa 'Alayhi salam and his people were running away from Pharaoh.", "And then they reached the sea point, and then there was the famous splitting of the sea happening by Moses, by the stick, by the command of Allah. So the people of Musa 'Alayhi salam said to him (Quran26:61-63) \"إِنَّا لَمُدْرَكُونَ\" “They were going to catch us”, they're going to kill us! Then Musa 'Alayhi salam said: \"كَلا إِنَّ مَعِيَ رَبِّي سَيَهْدِينِ\" “No, I have my Lord with me, Allah is with me and He will guide me the way”. Then Allahﷻ said: \"فَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ أَنِ اضْرِب بِّعَصَاكَ الْبَحْرَ ۖ فَانفَلَقَ فَكَانَ كُلُّ فِرْقٍ كَالطَّوْدِ الْعَظِيمِ \" “We said hit the sea with the stick, and then it's split, it’s like two mountains of waves”. Then when Musa 'Alayhi salam was crossing, Pharaoh followed them, even though he's seeing this with his own eyes! Imagine all of this: you see all of these miracles, you see it with your own eyes right now, the sea is split to two parts, two mountains, and you still follow; you want to kill Musa 'Alayhi salam after all of this. He followed behind Musa 'Alayhi salam, and then when Musa 'Alayhi salam crossed, now the sea’s closed in on Pharaoh and his people, and he was drowning.", "When he was dying, he tried to say: I believe. But, from the amount of arrogance, he didn't say: I believe in Allah; he said: \"I believe in the same God that the Children of Israel believed in\"! Look how long of a statement he made. He didn't even say \"I believe in God\", but because of his arrogance he said: \"I believe in the Lord that the Children of Israel believed in\". Then Allah said to him (Quran10:91) ءَاۤلۡـَٔـٰنَ وَقَدۡ عَصَیۡتَ قَبۡلُ وَكُنتَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُفۡسِدِینَ” “Is it now, when your soul is leaving your body, and you disobeyed before?” And some Scholars say that “disobey before” here is referring to him claiming to be God: so weren't you claiming to be God yesterday? Now when your soul is leaving your body, you're drowning, you're trying to say that I believe!", "So then Allahﷻ didn’t accept his repentance, because there's a condition in Islam that Allah mentions in chapter 4 (An-Nissa': Women) of the (Quran4:17-18). The beginning of chapter 4 is: “إِنَّمَا التَّوْبَةُ عَلَى اللَّهِ لِلَّذِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ السُّوءَ بِجَهَالَةٍ ثُمَّ يَتُوبُونَ مِن قَرِيبٍ” (Tawba [Repentance] is only for those who do the sins, then they repent before their death) “And the repentance is not for those who their soul is leaving their body”. If your soul is now leaving your body, now you already reached a point where you’re خلاص. So there's no point of you now to say: \"I believe\"; it's already done, you're dying. So in Islam, the test is open, the repentance is open until you're dying, your soul is leaving your body, which we call سكرات الموت (Sakarat El Mawt: Death throes), or the Sun rises from the opposite side, which is the sign of the Day of Judgment, the end of time; the test is over, it's the same thing. So unless these things happen, the person has a way to repent. And therefore that's why he was not saved by Allahﷻ. This story I'm telling you is from the Quran literally.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Man Realises The Contradictions In Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CR6_RG9qdVM", ((227, "3:47–4:38"), (282, "4:42–5:26"), (333, "5:33–6:09"), (373, "6:13–7:31"),))
