#passage(("Prophet Muhammadﷺ, even though he was trying his best, he still did things which God did not tell him to do in his life, but the Angels did not do anything like that. For example, one instance: a man came to Prophet Muhammadﷺ, a blind person; he wanted to learn from him about Islam, but Prophet Muhammadﷺ was speaking with the Heads of Mecca at the time. He was trying to convince them, or preach the Message to them, because if they believe, their people will also believe. So he saw the benefit there. When the man came to him, even though the man was blind, Prophet Muhammadﷺ frowned a little bit, then he turned away and talked to the people. Obviously the blind man didn't see him frowning, because he's a blind person. But Allahﷻ told him in the Quran that you frowned on that individual, but maybe that individual is seeking purification, maybe that individual is more worthy of you talking to him ('Abassa80:1-10). Human beings are not perfect.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Iceland Visitors Enquire About Islam! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xigQO8G9dOo", ((369, "6:09–7:04"),))
