#passage(("At times it was like he had little to nothing to say; my guess is that it's because he was shocked by some of the information that CP was presenting to him. Of course, upon fact-checking, we come to realize that he was lying through his teeth, as usual, and he was using that to catch his opponent off guard.", "The topic of the discussion was [muta], also known as temporary marriages. CP is arguing that chapter 4 verse 24 is about [muta]; the [sheikh] denies this. When pressed to provide an example of a commentary, he quotes [Alusi]. CP reads a statement that says \"it has been said that this verse is about [muta]\"; however, this is not [Alusi's] opinion. CP already changed the screen intentionally, in order to not allow him to catch the part where [Alusi] refutes him. The text translates to: the view that this verse was revealed about [muta] is wrong.", "CP claims that [Tabari] said that this verse is about [muta]. He says: and the more accurate of the two views is that this is to be understood as those that you get married, then have intercourse with, then pay them, referring to the dowry. CP claims that [Ibn Kathir] said that this verse is about muta. This is false as well: it actually says [Mujahid] said that this is about muta, but the majority of scholars are against this.",), "Farid Responds, “Christian Prince BUSTED by Azhar Shaikh! [Lies #95-98]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tMZvnnRWemE", ((18, "0:18–0:46"), (46, "0:46–4:01"), (258, "4:18–4:55"),))
