#passage(("So the point of them quoting the Hadith in the notes, without putting the full Hadith, but just putting the part that is relevant to the verse: the part that they want, which is relevant to the verse, is the part about burying children alive, because that's what the verse is referring to. The verse is saying that the disbelievers of Mecca, the Pagan Arabs, they say that the angels are the daughters of God. So they attribute daughters to God, but they themselves, they do not want daughters for themselves. Whenever they get news of a daughter, they hide from the people because they're ashamed, and then they bury those daughters alive. So Allahﷻ is saying: you yourself do not like daughters, and you're ashamed of daughters, and you bury them alive, but you attribute them to Allahﷻ, The Most High!", "And then the Hadith is saying that this is not acceptable at all, that you’re killing your children, burying them alive. And Allahﷻ says in the Quran also: (Attakwir81:8-9) وَإِذَا الْمَوْءُودَةُ سُئِلَتْ بِأَيِّ ذَنبٍ قُتِلَتْ (when baby girls, buried alive, are asked for what crime they were put to death). That child that has been buried, on the Day of Judgement it will question: What did I do for you to kill me? What sin did I do? What did I commit for you to bury me alive? That will happen on the Day of Judgement to the people who did that. That is the relevant part; that's why they mentioned the Hadith.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sister Cries After Realising Islam Is The Truth! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PtJpInP1jl8", ((398, "6:38–7:26"), (448, "7:28–7:52"),))
