#passage(("For those of you that didn't know, [Hany] is all about the stories of the Quran; he's always about these discoveries and these gifts, the mother of all gifts, that he's presenting to you, the viewer. So here's the thing: his interpretations conflict with traditional scholarship, like 180 degrees. But the thing is, naturally, after he comes up with his crazy interpretations, you're naturally going to go back to those books of tafsir, you're going to look into what the scholars have said, you're going to notice the conflicts. So what he does is he came up with a strategy, which is pretty much throw all the scholars under the bus. Oh, and by the way, he actually won't even allow you to mention a name of any of those scholars in the comments; he'd actually go ahead and delete those comments.", "Now, if we can't trust the translations, if we can't trust the books of exegesis, where are we going to go in order to understand the meanings of the Arabic of the Quran? Hani says that he has some things that you need to avoid; he gives you some guidelines. You can't rely on dictionaries, you can't rely on poetry, you can't extract meanings from classical poetry, you cannot rely on the language of seventh century Arabs; somehow the Quran is going to explain to you what it means. In any case, this guy uses his own methodology, and I use that word really loosely, in order to explain the stories of the Quran. By applying this methodology, Hani has come up to some new interpretations to the stories that we're all familiar with in the Quran. And remember, these are just a few of the examples; I've got tens of pages of notes, I just chose a few of them because these were some of the more interesting ones.", "So everyone's familiar with the story of Adam and his wife, and [Iblis] tempts them to eat from the tree, and they eat from the tree. But not really Iblis, because Iblis isn't a real thing. Oh, and by the way, [shajara] are apparently punks that like to argue. So one question comes to mind: why doesn't Allah use the name of Muhammad instead of Adam? Why doesn't he say the arguers, the debaters? Why doesn't he say those words? Now you see, Allah, the [All-Wise], is intentionally choosing those words, and what we find in the Quran looks similar to what we find in the Torah. You see, according to [Atchan], we're not supposed to believe in this stuff: we're not supposed to believe in the existence of the actual Adam, we're not supposed to believe in Eve, we're not supposed to believe in the tree, because all that's just Jewish folklore, according to him. But the Quran makes it seem like it's actually confirming those events. So [Atchan's] answer is: Allah is intentionally tricking us in order to get us to believe in these folktales.", "Remember the story about Musa and the wife [of Pharaoh], where she takes him in as a baby? Well, apparently you got it a bit wrong. And you actually thought it was the wife that saved him? No, that's not what happened: it was actually one of [Pharaoh's] female gang members. Oh, by the way, do you know what tribe [Pharaoh] is from? Actually from Bani Israel, which is apparently Beni Moussa, whatever. Oh, and by the way, [Pharaoh] used to have spies everywhere; however, luckily another gangster used to run around and kill the spies.", "Now, just to refresh your memory, remember how [Atchan] was saying that the prophet, peace be upon him, is Adam? Well, there are a few more twists in the story. So they purposefully hid this. And this is very important, especially if you're a fan of [Atchan]; I want you to think about this: who are they? Who is he speaking about? Is this referring to scholars of tafsir? Because that's what it seems like. And the thing is, [Atchan] is claiming that this is his own discovery, this methodology, something that he uncovered. Now, if it's something that he uncovered, how are they hiding this information, if they didn't know of this information? Think about that. Here's the thing: what is their motivation for doing this? To make the Quran on the same levels as other books? Why? Who said so? What's the [dalil]? Where's the proof of this? These are Muslim scholars of the Quran that adhere to the Quran and place it above everything else. That's challenge number one to Hani: bring evidence; name one scholar that believed that Muhammad is Ismail. So the prophet, peace be upon him, didn't teach this methodology. So if even the prophet, peace be upon him, didn't teach this methodology, then how come these scholars have hid this information, if they never even knew of the methodology? Once again, these are your discoveries.",), "Farid Responds, “Exposing Hany Atchan (Marvelous Quran)”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y_BpFzMJgX0", ((342, "5:42–8:59"), (560, "9:20–12:47"), (777, "12:57–17:12"), (1041, "17:21–19:10"), (1224, "20:24–23:35"),))
