// U ML280:50-112 | The Muslim Lantern | 8
#passage(("In Islam there's different sciences. For example, there's the Science of Tafseer: Tafseer is exegesis, explanation of the Quran. So the Quran being explained, the verses, the context, the reason for Revelation, all of that: that's one science. Another science is the Science of Hadith: the transmission, the narrations from the Prophetﷺ, what he said, what he did, etc. Another science, for example, is the Sira: is the biography, history. So we have books of history, and each of these sciences have their own criterias.", "The books of Tafseer (exegesis) and the books of history, they have a lot of information that was hearsay, that is being said in the community, that they were recorded in their books. They would not only rely on authentic information that has been transmitted and established to be historically accurate. While, on the other hand, some books of Hadith will only rely on Authentic Narrations; they will not add anything else. So they will look at the Chain Of Narration, the individuals passing the information: are they reliable or not? And after investigation, they will say: we accept this information. So in books of Sira or in books of Tafseer, you will find certain things mentioned that are not accurate.", "Even the person who wrote the book himself, the book of exegesis, like Attabari, who's one of the biggest classical exegesists, he says in his book, in the introduction: \"You will find certain things in this book that are completely repulsive. But we're just reporting history; we're not looking for the authentic things and giving you the authentic information there.\" So this is what he says. He's saying hearsay, people saying things here and there, so we record hearsay of the people.", "Now this story, you can find in certain books, books of Tafseer, this and that. And all the scholars, the scholars of Hadith, the scholars of exegesis in Islam, will say this story is completely fabricated. It does not have a single Chain Of Narration that is authentic.", "Now if anyone would further investigate, at least he needs to have some little level knowledge of Arabic, I would say. Because there is a book written (I can recommend) by Sheikh Al-Albani, who's a great scholar of the Science of Hadith, the Science Of Narrations, recognizing what is authentic and what is not. He wrote a whole book about this story. It's called: \"نصبُ المَجانيق لنسفِ قصّة الغَرانيق\" (Erecting the Catapults to blast the story of the Gharaneeq). It is an attack on the story. So all the book presents why the story is fabricated, could not be true, could not be historically reliable, giving you multiple reasons for why this is the case.", "The story contradicts the Quran in many ways. For example, the Quran says that this book is preserved (Alhijr15:9), and Allah sends angels protecting the Revelation when the Quran is coming down. So no one can insert anything in the Quran or outside the Quran (Aljinn72:27-28). So Allahﷻ says (Fussilat41:41-42): إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ بِٱلذِّكْرِ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ وَإِنَّهُۥ لَكِتَٰبٌ عَزِيزٌ (Those who disbelieve in the Quran when it came to them, and it is a mighty book) لَّا يَأْتِيهِ ٱلْبَٰطِلُ مِنۢ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَلَا مِنْ خَلْفِهِۦ تَنزِيلٌ مِّنْ حَكِيمٍ حَمِيدٍ (Falsehood does not approach it from in front of it or from the side or from behind). Or anywhere: falsehood cannot enter this Revelation. So these explicit, clear-cut verses of the Quran contradict this story. Therefore this story cannot be accurate from an Islamic perspective.", "And we are narrating the story, by the way. We are telling you the story! That's why we are telling you: because if we're trying to hide something, we're not going to have the story in the books. But we're narrating the story, and we tell you that we're not hiding from anything, but the fact is that this story is not historically reliable.", "Where are the reliable Muslim Scholars that authenticated this story? According to your understanding as well! Because they can say the story is authentic and give a different understanding to what you think.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Claims The Quran Contains Satanic Verses?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=27xa01f05ag", ((179, "2:59–3:15"), (202, "3:22–3:45"), (230, "3:50–4:07"), (251, "4:11–4:52"), (295, "4:55–5:18"), (322, "5:22–5:56"), (359, "5:59–6:07"), (384, "6:24–6:28"),))
