// U ML227:518-576 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("So this is a story called the story of Gharaniq, and it's specifically in the surah of the Qur'an called Surat anNajm. And there is a verse there in which there is a prostration done. And then there is a narration in the books of history that mentions that, when the verse was said, the next verse after it was تلك الغرانيق العلا وأن شفاعتهن لا ترتجى (These are the great idols or great gods), after mentioning the name of the gods. Allah says originally in the Surah (anNajm53:23): \"These are only names that you've invented\". Now, you've got history that says: \"No, it didn't say that these are all the names that you've invented. What actually was said...\" (these verses that you're saying that came from Satan) \"...that these are great gods and we should seek their forgiveness\", or something like that.", "We have an authentic version of it that does not mention that, which is in Bukhari. So when you have narrations narrated, and the people narrating it are the strongest of memorisers and most reliable of individuals, then you have the same story narrated by someone who is not strong or reliable, adding more details, you already know that this is something that has been fabricated and added by incorrect sources. So we already have the same story in Bukhari, but it does not include that, in which we can know that these reliable people, better memorizers and more reliable people, did not mention that detail. Therefore, this did not happen.", "Also, Allah told the Prophetﷺ: \"When the revelation is told, do not hasten to recite it (TaHa20;114). First, internalise it. When you're done, Allah will preserve it in your heart, then recite it\". So it was not like these two verses came and the Prophetﷺ straight away said it, because there is a way that Allah told the Prophetﷺ to accept and take the revelation. Now, on top of that as well, the place where you prostrate is actually in the end of the Surah, in the end of the chapter; it is not where the names of the idols are mentioned. So that is another reason that shows inconsistency to the story.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Compares Islam And Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Igzqbqr2Pew", ((1851, "30:51–31:37"), (1940, "32:20–32:50"), (2013, "33:33–33:57"),))
